#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if Marius found out about it...she wondered how he'd take it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a menacing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if he faces me in battle, I will spare not a soul."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if he knew, he gave no hint of it. And his estimation of her never wavered."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily revealing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if he lied, she would be beyond the walls. Nobody would be able to come save her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with a hint of caution
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "But if her offer is genuine, you might accidentally give offense by refusing her invitation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if her thoughts moved slow, her words were even worse."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if his offer was true..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if it kept the peace, maybe it was worth it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if it meant no more blood...it would be worth it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful, with a hint of skepticism
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if it wanted her dead, it could have done so easily by now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprisingly apologetic
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if it's space you're looking for, maybe I'll ask the captain if you can sleep in his cabin."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if more waves of refugees come...I don't know."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if she did step up and save these women, the soldiers would forever remember her as the woman that denied them their spoils of war."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if she had done any of these things, Sarah truthfully could not recall."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a confident, assured tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if she showed him, he could no longer deny it..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously uneasy
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if something were to happen to you there...I don't think I'd be able to forgive myself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly accepting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if that was what it took to get his help, she'd accept it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly incredulous
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if the Khan finds out...won't he be angry?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "But if the council asks..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if the spirit's words were true..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Old Tribesman"
msgid "But if they see me take you..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But if they so much as harm a hair on your head..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Concernedly anxious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But if they were discovered, it could mean they'd be detected."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a concerned and earnest tone
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "But if they're slaves for too long they become exhausting. They don't use their brains for years on end, so they all but end up losing them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if tonight is all we have, can't that be enough?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But if we manage to score a clean hit with one of the cannons, it could turn the entire fortress into an inferno."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if we only did the things that come easy to us, we'd never grow or learn to challenge ourselves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "But if you ask me, I think it's a good thing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Incredulously amazed
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "But if you had seen this girl's ass, I swear you would have-"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "But if you learn your place in this new land, you can carve out a good life. I promise you this."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "But if you make me walk out of here, unsatisfied...well I might just be sad about that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, detached tone
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "But if you reject his claim, he can pretend that he never named Oliver at all, and then Oliver will have less grounds to be offended."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if you so much as leave a mark on my body, the smallest of bruises, I will go to my brother."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Menacingly warning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if you touch a hair on my brother's head, your suffering will be a thousand times worse!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously amused
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "But if you try to use a hammer to saw a board in half, it's gonna be terrible."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "But if you want to keep your army, I suggest you don't."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "But if you want, I shall tell you tales of what he did to me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously amused
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "But if you're a punk..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But if you're here to escort me..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in a sense, they had their own beauty because of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reflecting, with a hint of nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in all her dreams there was single fact."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "But in between the rocks, there is space."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached amusement
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "But in case you're a bit slow, blondie, I'll make sure you get it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in days that turned to weeks, he began to train her more diligently."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in every direction of the city, Sarah could see the shapeless shadows."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense and alert
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in fleeting flashes of realization, she could see the wrinkles on his body, reminding her of what he was."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in her dreams, she never thought of the violence."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in his arms..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in his eyes, only wonder."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Enthusiastically, excitedly
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "But in my world, it was abundant. The Three Sisters gave it freely to all who desired it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Inquisitively explaining
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "But in our lessons, I have often tried to impart that there is more to life than just work."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in that place, something occured to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With increasing concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in the cauldron below, the emotions of her people climbed ever higher."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a passionate, urgent whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in the end, the grinding motion continued to build, driving her over the edge."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But in the end, there were also those who rebelled because their farms had failed and their children were hungry."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in the end, they seemed happy, and Sarah wondered how anyone could really object to that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "But in the jungle, they were meaningless. They could not march and fight on open plains, only enter and be slowly strangled by the cursed place."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in the midst of all that loneliness, it was a tempting idea. A friend."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued and hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in the midsts of all that destruction, she saw people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in the weeks after, as she found her heart grow closer to Atilla's, she discovered the opposite."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently assuring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in this moment it wasn’t a lie."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly reciting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in this moment, it seemed to Sarah like the most delicious of things."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "But in this place, certain things are expected of women, same as they are of men."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in this plaza, the largest of them all, was Naelyon."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in time, she began to feel warmth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with reassurance
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in time, they found their way."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, detached tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in truth, she barely knew Garret."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in truth, the tribesmen wanted to guard their wealth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But in what state?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But inside of her body, a maddening pulse of pleasure had taken over."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly fondly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead of resolving it, she simply remained nestled in his loving arms."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead that perhaps, the pain of her loss, though deep, would not prove fatal."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, Sarah found on her face the same expression she found on most slaves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, Sarah only felt a primal heat."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Emotionally detached delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, for how little it seemed to mean to her. How cold all of it left her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "But instead, he died here. At the end of the fucking world in some town that nobody remembers."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Stern disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, she moaned for him like a whore."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sardonically amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, she was his wife."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a thoughtful, contemplative manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, she was left mostly unharmed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, uninterested tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, she was nobody here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, she would be empowering the army of her closest neighbour."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But instead, this place was just a hidden valley, with its own unique climate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But instead..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly, with resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But instead...her death was quick and sudden."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But is it powerful?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But is my position so strange?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it  was moments like these where Sarah reminded herself that for as much as she had changed, she still craved some parts of her easier, previous life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it also drew her in, in ways that Sarah herself found hard to be conscious of. She sometimes found herself staring at the princess, her flawless features, her lithe frame."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a deeply saddened whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it also felt more hollow for it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it also holds the smallest army and the smallest population from which to draft an army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it also reminded her of what it had cost her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, puzzled tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it also seems to avoid humans to a degree. It doesn't go into the town. So why? Why attack outside the forest at all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, neutral delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it also wouldn't matter."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But it can take you to the throne room, the council, the gardens, the kitchens even."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Concerned, questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it cannot last."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it could do nothing to stop the flame."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it did not cut the air, rather, it cut deeper still."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it did."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it didn't come."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and tender
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it didn't matter to Kate. Kate simply held her as she wept."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it didn't matter, she thought."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly stating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it didn't matter."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it didn't matter. She had done what she had to do to survive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly indifferent
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it didn't matter. The cart rushed forward and before she knew it, they had passed over the small bridge and were clear on the other side."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "But it doesn't feel like it did before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it doesn't matter. What matters is putting a stop to this insurrection and getting Thomas back."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly lamenting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it drank in her energy, as if it had been starving for a century."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it endured."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, wistful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it faded away just as quickly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Abruptly surprised
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it had all happened so fast."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it had been so long ago now, it seemed almost absurd to say it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it had brought her little joy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, almost somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it hadn't been long before she realized that it had all been pretend."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it hadn't just been a feeling. People who witnessed her magics, feared her. Even the smallest pale flame could cause men to back away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "But it has happened on occasion, so I think the risk is still important to know."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "But it is equally possible the enemy knows this."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it is in times of great crisis, like the one we find ourselves in, that we are forced to confront the simple truths."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a fervent, hopeful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it is my wish, my desire, above all, to return back home. Back to Rosanna."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it is only you and I who will ever really know each other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally, with slight confusion
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it meant nothing to Sarah or her husband, because a coward that didn't even dare to utter a curse in public, was no threat at all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it never did. Instead, each of the slaves yearned for the same thing all others did."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it only added to the spectacle, as among the embers, Samayra moved untouched and without missing a single step."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "But it really started when they were ordered to leave their loot behind."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "But it seems you've made yourself busy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Mildly disappointed sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was a pale flame that burned her dreams."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was a pointless shame, she realized."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and distant
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was a soft comfort."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised and curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was a whisper in a huricane."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "But it was also a life free from challenge. Free from hard work."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was also easy for her to forget that at the end, he was loyal to this place. These people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was also kind of cute and romantic, that this brute of a man had put actual thought into it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Relentlessly furious
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "But it was blood money to me. I sought out the orc that had killed my wife, and I bashed in his head with his father's gold."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it was by fate and foolishness that Vaelen drove me to this moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confusedly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was clear to Sarah that it was none of these things. Belmont's intentions were real."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was different than in Bagrad."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was finally the nation of Mythra, that broke the cycle."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was her or him, and Sarah knew that in this world, she'd choose herself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative haze
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was impossible to think in this moment. Each thought was interrupted moments after it formed by another spank."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was impossible, so numerous."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively somber
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was in moments like these where Sarah felt guilty for the void that she had made out of her heart."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "But it was just enough to keep us fed and keep the house over our head."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In awe, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it was me..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was not like the sky as she knew it all. So vast and so plentiful, the stars bathed the sky in a cold blue light."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was only Sakar and Krip."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemnly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was rare for her to feel connected with anyone the way she felt with Kate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Ayaka"
msgid "But it was the opposite."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was the truth. He wasn't even old enough to be her father, more like a grandfather."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was those base desires that she could play to."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tone of concern and urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was too dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was too late for pleading now. The sentence had been spoken and there would be no going back."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it was warm, and once eaten, it warmed the body. Sarah would do anything for some heat, even shovel down this slob."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't Nick's size, or lack thereof, that had struck Sarah in this moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't a chaos."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively listening
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't her mother, she realized, only that now, dressed in this wedding dress and made to look so much a woman, Sarah recognized her mother's features in herself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't just a question of handling them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptically intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:King Orwell Rose"
msgid "But it wasn't like that at all. Everywhere I went, it was the same thing. People talking about a man called Hassar."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't long before Sarah felt her husband stirring again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't long before the goblin opened the cage to the door and stepped inside."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflecting on a distant past
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "But it wasn't long before the other Gods likewise decided to cross that line."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it wasn't right, that man was-"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't that, Sarah now realized. She was more shocked of Sarah's nakedness than any magical threats."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily, with a hint of resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wasn't to be so."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Authoritatively confident
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it will be my soldiers, acting on my word."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "But it will. Things are already changing, after you took over from Vaelen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Passively supportive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it would be smarter to give herself, she reasoned."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber tone, with resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it would end today."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, warily
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "But it would not be anything as brutal as what the Tribesmen impose."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "But it wouldn't be right."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But it wouldn't matter. Not if they were too late."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously confident
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But it's also just a fort."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "But it's always a waiting game."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it's been a long road since."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Nathan"
msgid "But it's better than most."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously hopeful, yet apprehensive
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it's fine...well, not this but...I think I can manage my emotions. At least for the night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with a hint of nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "But it's going to be a long night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, with fondness
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But it's grown on me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "But it's late, they're gonna wonder where we are, it's a long story, and honestly, you tired me out."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
