msgid "But then, Sarah felt her heart steel."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then, amidst it all, she also felt the other sensation."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then, disaster…"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then, she had been in the audience."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly, with warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then, she had come to love that as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then, slowly, as it had before, the mist began to swirl and dance forth from the flask."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then, what was she to do?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, with slight uncertainty
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But then..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding thoughtfully
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "But there are advantages to being the Captain."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "But there are also creatures that are more...amicable to control."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently assured
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "But there are many ways for myself to benefit, and for you to benefit as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Concerned, yet calm delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Advisor"
msgid "But there are many who speak of the Orc threat-"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "But there are not infinite potential paths."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "But there are other dangers. Certain parts of the forest are so thick they barely allow you to even make camp."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But there are other places in the world that you could go to, couldn't you? Many places that would value your talents."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "But there are plenty of staff that do."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Quietly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But there don't have to be..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But there is a condition, Marion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "But there is a difference between knowing something and believing it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively somber
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "But there is also a pain in my heart. An absence that I feel, as surely as all of you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "But there is one more thing!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there seemed a real buzz in the air."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was a difference, Sarah now realized."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was also simply her husband the man, who beneath all other pretense, also simply desired her for her body, and she was eager for his."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was also something else, though she found it hard to put her finger on."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was an ease to the submission."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was another glimme there too."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mixture of surprise and concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was no blood."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was no disgust to be found in her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was no pretending, not during the act. Only after when she had regained her sanity could she feign innocence to herself, until the next time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was nobody."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was none of the rejection that Sarah knew in her heart she deserved."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somber resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was nowhere to go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a cautiously intrigued tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was one danger."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, restrained tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was only so much that reason could tell her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was only the solid wall of stone in front of her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was something else here too."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued and sensing mystery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was something in his face that Sarah seemed to recognize, though she couldn't quite put her finger on it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was something still odd about him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative tone, with a hint of disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there was the idea of it, and then there was the truth of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a tone of resigned frustration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there wasn't much space for her to go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Relievedly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But there were plenty of deaths on both sides. And near the end, even the City Guard wanted to end the conflict."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there would be no answer."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somber reflection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But there would be no turning of time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "But these are all mostly other cleaning staff, so you'd do good to get along with them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense, foreboding whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But these beasts seemed to be moved by only destruction."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But these beasts were entirely different."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But these men were eager for a good death."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "But these proposals will stand centuries."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But these were clearly different from the breeds she had grown up with."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "But they are few in numbers compared to those who are still left behind. Trapped and at the mercy of the Tribes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But they are loyal. They tell me what I want to hear. Not always what I need to hear."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, thoughtful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "But they are only inherent to the nature of their own world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they blamed them for how meekly they allowed it all to happen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they couldn't be foolish."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Firmly convinced
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they couldn't run away, for the throne room had only one way out, and Sarah would not let them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense relief
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they had burned what little Hugh had gifted them, so they had to wait for when he returned again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they had each other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously anticipating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they had equally come too close to Sarah's army to simply retreat, fearing a rain of arrows in their back."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly, with a hint of frustration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they had fallen short."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Incredulous shock
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But they have not yet been equipped. Hells, they haven't even begun to their basic training."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But they have their limits."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But they look alike enough, so maybe that's it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they spotted no sight or sound of the Orcs or Goblins."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "But they start thinkin of that when they get too comfortable."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they understood power."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they understood that this was not needed. The message had been send, and all understood."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Annoyed skepticism
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they were always vile, ruthless and stupid."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "But they were amateurs. They take one look at me and they don't even bother."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a proud, confident tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they were battle-hardend warriors."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "But they were blind to one fact."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "But they were known to practice flesh weaving. Unnatural creatures could still roam in the deepest pits of this place."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they were meaningless voices, compared to the immediate pleasure of serving him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they were met out on the open fields, and their raw strength proved no match for the modern warfare of the Mythran armies."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly contemplating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they were out of position, and from above them, she could easily burn more of them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they were still skilled warriors and hunters, known for raiding and capturing slaves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "But they were wrong only once, and the world paid for it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But they weren't real stories. Nothing he had experienced for himself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they would remember him for as long as they lived."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they would survive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But they would wait for her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "But they're also...lonely...I think."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective observation
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "But they've also been here for a few years."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly realizing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "But things are different now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disheartened acceptance
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But things were dire enough, Sarah would take any help."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly encouraging
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "But this can be your workstation."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this caused no conflict in the world of the Tribesmen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But this city is pretty big, and it doesn't have slaves at all..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this early morning, he wanted to feel her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this group had been the people nearer to the market. The busiest section of the city."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this had been what Xan had warned her about, years ago."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached bemusement
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this hardly felt like a battle. This felt like the end of something."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "But this is not who he is. His every performance is meant to deceive you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But this is the truth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But this is what I've really missed these last few days."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a curious observing manner
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "But this one."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this place alone, stood apart."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "But this place...this Empire, this city..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflecting fondness
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this room, and this desk, this had been the center of his studies, and with it, the center of his world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "But this thing is like no animal I have ever encountered. It outsmarts us, and it doesn't even seem to kill for food."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this time, Sarah turned her blade."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this too was a part of ruling."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a confident, authoritative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "But this town is practically a fort. They don't dare to come near."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was a new world for Sarah. Here, her title didn't mean much of anything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was a world ruled by strength."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptically doubtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was different from before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was different, soft and considerate, words that did not describe her master."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nostalgically reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was different."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly revealing a secret
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was more than just an orgy of flesh."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was no ordinary dagger, rather, its blade shined with a deep crimson red light. A colour she had only ever seen once before in her life, earlier that day."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was nothing like that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was something else. No matter how skilled they were, they could not defeat this many people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was the right decision. Sarah couldn't allow herself to be distracted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this was their bargain, she thought."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding slowly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this woman was different, Sarah realized."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached cynicism
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But this world makes poor men soldiers, and poor women whores."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But this world...it's dead. What is left of it?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a sense of dawning realization
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But this, she soon learned, was little more than an optical illusion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But this..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tiredly pleading
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But this...Kate, you have to stop doing this to yourself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective sorrow
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "But those old wounds...they never fully healed. This disease, the addiction, it's inside of me in a way I can't explain."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Amused, warmly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But those stories usually ended when they kissed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disgustingly sarcastic
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "But those were idiots. Too stupid to realize what or who they were dealing with."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But those were in battle. This...I have never murdered an innocent for so calous a reason."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Quietly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But those would be considerations to come in years after."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But though he grew older, the work only seemed lighter to him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassured
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But though she had not joined them, they had never harmed her either."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly condescending
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "But though they favored her as well, they refused."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly revealing, with slight weariness
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "But through a warped lense, their kind intentions can be...twisted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But through half-closed eyes, Sarah could see Kate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to Sarah it had seemed only logical. A way to break through the same old way of ruling."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to Sarah, it passes in a blur."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contentedly accepting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to Sarah, the scars on Kate's body were not off-putting."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued and reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to carry on her body an indelible mark, showing her to be his property forever..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to compare herself to her Father still seemed to her mind as blasphemous."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to her body, there was little distinction."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to her own surprise, she felt something else slide off her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to her, the children never appeared her own."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But to instead govern as you see fit."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disenchanted resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to instead, exist as animals in heat."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised and curious
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "But to my surprise, she was all but naked beneath her sheets!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplative with a hint of nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to now be here, alone, with her husband..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to see the injury on the girl. The pain in the Mayor's face. It all struck much closer to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "But to see you walkin about here, wearin my late wife's clothes..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to these cretins, it was like home, and they knew the way by heart."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "But to this, the gods did not agree."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "But to those in positions of state, or a bank like my family operates, you learn that money is just a number on a piece of paper."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mixture of sadness and resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But to those of you who remain..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively earnest
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "But to us, there is only strength that matters. Those who have it. And those who don't."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But today was a different day."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively lost in thought
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But today, her thoughts were otherwise occupied."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally informative
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "But tonight is going to be more of a lesson."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But tonight, at least, there is nobody here but us."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "But tonight, they will worship you like the heroes you are! Like the warriors you are! Like the conquerors of history that you are!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively curious
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But tonight, we both saw what kind of a man he is."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nobly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But towering over all of them, the castle of Queen Maeiv, the central seat of power that sat itself at the center of the city."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But trapped beneath him, Sarah could not deny the ways of her own body either."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Incredulously puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But tricking me as well? Why? You didn't need to do that. Just so you could make a fool out of me?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "But truth is I just like to watch your ass and tits."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But try to remember this place. These people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly consoled
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "But unfortunately, I must dissapoint you. I know little more than you do, it seems."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With eager curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But unlike any mixture she had ever drank, she could continue to feel it as it made its way into her body."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "But unlike them, my father had taken me to the provincial capital."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tentatively amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But until now, I never thought I'd call you cute."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly assertive
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "But we are honest men of the law, and we don't let your kind run free."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "But we cannot be seen disagreeing in public."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Pensive and uncertain
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But we don't know anything...maybe I don't have any magical abilities."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily uncertain
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But we drove them back."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "But we get news, here and there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Firmly resolved
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "But we have a great obligation, and we cannot stray from that. We must keep our eyes on the great mission."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "But we need to leave tonight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily explaining
msgctxt "speaker:Merchant"
msgid "But we only ever offered to transport his goods, not bear all risk. We would never have agreed to such a thing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "But we were in bed and he...asked me to fetch him some wine from the basement."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With warmth and encouragement
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "But we will do it together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently with pride
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "But we won in so far as that we are not all in chains."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Triumphant, encouraging
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But we won't fail!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Motivationally hopeful, reassuringly comforting
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But we'll get through this, you and me. And whenever things get too much, remember that I'm here for you. Always."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But we're his advisors. Isn't it our job to keep him from making a mistake like this?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "But what I felt for you...it never left me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determinedly defiant
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what I will not do, is let myself be bound by their small judgements."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what about Daemonology?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what about everything else?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what about the both of you? You're here about that magical pulse as well?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what about the offer of Gilead to help me? Should I take it?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what about the rest?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But what about you?"
msgstr ""

