msgstr ""

#. emotion: Passionately committed
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That is what we offer. A steady hand. And that is what I do, and some others. We are agents of that steady hand, seeking to implement this project of peace."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is what you are, no?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "That is why I issued an order to replace the current Governor for the Eastern Provinces."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, with assurance
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "That is why I say that we can make this work...for the both of us."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "That is why I wanted to talk to you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is why I'm still here, Duke Antonio."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "That is why our world has remained in such a state of decline."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That is why we leave the totems, to remind them of their old lives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That is, supposing you are still interested in learning more of the book."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is...you speak the language of the Tribes?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "That isn't why I called you over."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with encouragement
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That it might just be. Still, you should be celebrating."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That it was Xan who was doing it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That it's you! Xan had told me so much about you, his new apprentice."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding in sympathy
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That just cost you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprisingly delighted
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That just happened to be yours."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With restrained admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That kind of softness was something she couldn't afford in her current life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That kinda connection...that's always gonna cost ya."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Dispassionately, with a hint of sorrow
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That knowledge had lost its use when her homeland fell, and most houses she could name were now either snuffed out or living as refugees."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a concerned, urgent whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That leaves the palace almost entirely undefended. There will be a handful of guards left, but that's it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached and introspective
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That leaves you with only your own."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly speaking
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That lithe frame, mixed with the strong muscles, hers was truly a body in its prime."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, with mild disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That little?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued yet concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That long, without food?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That long?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly with detachment
msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "That looked like a nasty fall."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That looked more natural on him than the nervousness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a warm, approving tone
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "That looks decent enough."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With growing excitement and wonder
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That magical pulse. Don't tell me you can't feel it?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "That makes sense"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a confident nod
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That makes sense. I really should have figured that out myself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That makes sense...I think."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "That man...that man that served you your drink, and your food, he used to be little more than a farmhand and a thief."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That many."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a curious observing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That many?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That maybe if we picked up on where we left off years ago, I could be all quiet like about it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That means I'll take you on as an apprentice."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "That means leaving everyone except the capital, defenseless. If Hassar avoids the capital, and attacks another district, they'll only have women and children to defend themselves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "That means no fights. No drugs. No trouble."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Historically reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That means they were there when the old Empire fell."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Deliberately confident
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That means you must govern not just from your heart, but also from what is right for the country."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously amused
msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Prince"
msgid "That means you're free to leave. Even if I suspect you probably killed more than a few of my men."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That meant bringing them over to her side. For some that was inspiring their hearts, but for many more it was simply filling their greed and urges."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That men were of such nature, and women of another nature, and this justified all the ways in which they were treated differently."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "That might last you longer than you think."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That might not mean anything to you, but it does to me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, almost reverent tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That moment is now, in this place..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That moment on the balcony just keeps haunting me and I can't do anything about it!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That moment when all she needed to do was be present, for him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Earnestly encouraging
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That money would be far better spend on the needy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That morning she had awoken as a princess, and before the sun had fully set, she was now a slave."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a sarcastically mocking tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That moron!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "That much is clear, but why did you lose? Why are you now offering your body to the man that destroyed your nation?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "That much is probably true. I'll go and see about uniform, give me a moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Relievedly affirming
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That much is true."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That much was the truth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That much, Sarah knew to be true. For every king and emperor in her world, there were millions who simply toiled away their lives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with a hint of sarcasm
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "That nobody really knows what they're doing. No truly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a resigned whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That nobody would ever know how she had given in to him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Harshly disdainful chuckle
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That obnoxious booming laugh of his."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That once, rivers flowed and carried with them life. Fields of grass and grain, spoiling the citizens of the nation with plenty."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That one over, not under. The rope gets pulled up this way, and leans across that part. You wrap them up, you risk it snapping at high winds."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "That one was a deviant as well. I got rid of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That over there was the town square, but you might a figured that out."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That part also belonged to him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Passionately exuding confidence
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That part was clearly virile."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That people could live so freely...and confusingly...it was a lot for her to make sense of."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That perhaps it was as simple as the fact that she wanted him, no other conditions."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somber reflection
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That place had nothing left for me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With cautious intrigue
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That place was no doubt dangerous. Going in at dark was not something she was planning for."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, accusatory tone
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That poor peasant girl, whipped on your command."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That power, his iron muscles, the way he could so easily throw her around, thinking about it, Sarah felt herself get wet."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber reflection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That promise, of war, then comfort, had now been crudely violated by Vaelen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That reminded her. She had been so busy lately, she had let her prayers slip."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively pointing out
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That reminds me, I need to get one of my tools from the cabin, that will make it easier to show you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disgustingly contemptuous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That rough and violent desire, mixed with that arrogant disregard that he had for her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That same brutal winter landscape that had ruined her last time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That same false smile. Those same cruel eyes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense, foreboding whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That same night, they also murdered every remote branch of that family."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Shah Mahda"
msgid "That seems to be about all I ever purchased from you, despite everything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding in approval
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That seems to fit."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "That settles the matter of Hassar and the desert tribes. What is left on the agenda for today?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That sex between a husband and a wife, like all skills, was one honed over time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly warning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That shame will follow your family's name until the end of times."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she could manipulate him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she had lost something that had never been hers to begin with?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she had permission."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised yet skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she would do anything, literally anything, if it meant that he might call her that again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued and slightly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she would take off her clothes and reveal nothing other than her ordinary body."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she, the young and beautiful woman, was like a gift to the old man, for which he should be grateful."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a delighted, almost astonished tone
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That smells amazing!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemn concern
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That somehow sounds even worse."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a curious and slightly hopeful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That somehow, despite everything she knew about him, he would prove a hero."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That sounds awful."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That sounds familiar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "That sounds horrible."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That sounds horrible."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a warm, understanding tone
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "That sounds like a problem for the two of you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "That sounds nice."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That sounds nice."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That sounds pretty bleak."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That stuf...was..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sorrowfully nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That such a flower should belong to another family, when it looks so good on you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That summer, shipment after shipment of grain arrived in the nearby town, collapsing the price."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That the death of their Khan had caused them to fall back to infighting."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That the one true ambition of Maeiv had been this last and final proposal."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That the real work was done in the shadows."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "That there is Edgar."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "That there is Pale Eclips, what I use for my cartography."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a warm, admiring tone
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "That there is a proper glass of wine. Or at least as proper as you're going to find in these here slums."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, thoughtful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That there is shoreline."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That there is the last housing block that is still standing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That there was some part of herself that didn't fully live in this world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tone of wonder and slight hesitation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That there would be more here than mere lust."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That they could make so much money off just one cart seemed absurd to Sarah."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly revealing, with a touch of sympathy
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That they were not all so different, and that they likewise lived upon the edge between surviving and ruin."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That they were somehow the same."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nostalgically reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "That time it was one of the carpenter's apprentices. Boy lost his entire left hand but at least he lived to tell about it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That time passed, she could only faintly tell because the light of the sun slowly turned and then darkened."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hushed, hopeful whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That time will come."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Annoyed disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That title of yours...the Silent Queen...I don't think it fits."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That too, but I also think you got potential."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low, cautionary tone
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "That trade official was a big softy, but plenty of those people up there are ruthless."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a sorrowful, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That type of stuff should be between people that love each other. I don't love you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That underneath all the pretense and protocol, the world, and the people in it, are reduced to their nature."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "That understanding ultimately led me to...well, you know our history."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a weary, detached tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That use also no longer mattered."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In awe and admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was Atilla to her. The surface, and the deeper version of him. The real truth that only she knew about."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Alertly concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was a dangerous thing in a place like this."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was a lifetime ago."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm reflection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was about all that she could say for it. No luxury. Nothing that made it seem like there was any personal touch to it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was about all there was to the sparsely decorated room."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was all it took. And in return he would give her so much more."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was an idea that did seem to appeal to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was an insane amount of money for anything, let alone a drink."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That was back then. We ain't doin nothing you don't wanna do now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, scholarly tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was before they went to war with the Mythran empire, centuries ago."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, almost indifferent tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was enough for her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was essentially all of it. From a princess, down to this."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was far from how the people of Rosanna lived."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective gratitude
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was her weapon, she realized. The means by which she could bend a man like him to her own will."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was him, she thought. Those two parts, the desire mixed in with his hesitant tenderness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pensive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was his curse, Sarah thought. If her brother had simply not cared, or been lazier, he wouldn't have demanded so much from himself. He wouldn't push himself this hard."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtful contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was it, Sarah thought."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contented, satisfied sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was it, she realized."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was it. Her one ally. Her one resource."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That was it. That abominable mage..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Condescendingly, as if pitying the listener
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That was just...foolishness, captain."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That was more than five years ago. I thought they had killed the entire royal family."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pensive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was one thing about soldiers, Sarah thought, at least they knew to keep to themselves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was something she could give him, she had decided."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That was something..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was the life she had been preparing for back then. The game of politics."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tone of detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was the not the wound that a soldier might have given her. It was more like something a wild animal might do."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and somber
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was the only fraction of comfort she had. The knowledge that the creature would pay, in time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm and contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was their biggest difference, Sarah knew."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative and somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That was true when you found me in the alley too."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was true, but Sarah also knew what Samayra likely hinted at."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was until its ruler, Shah Mahda, had accidentally caused the death of a Mythran prince during a fight at a party."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Dispassionately observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was what all these nights had done to her. He had trained her, and unknowingly, she had allowed herself to be trained to his desires."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was what passed for privacy and politeness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Resigned, wistfully
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "That was why I could never bring myself to ask you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously worried
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was worse."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "That was years ago."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was, until Xan told Sarah that they were going to offer the city their protection."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplative pause
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That was, until a thought came to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That was...how did you do that?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective wonderment
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That was...something else."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly, yet amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That wasn't funny!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised denial
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That wasn't my fault!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hushed, tenderly curious tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That way that only he could make her feel."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a confident, reassuring tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That way, no matter what, I will be safe."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Passionately proud
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "That we as leaders of our respective nations are bound to uphold a duty to our people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, with pride
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That we can do."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a hint of excitement, eagerly speaking
msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "That we do. A few open actually, there is a nice one that has a view of the plaza outside."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That whatever this latest act is, it comes only after a long series of debasements."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a condescending, mocking tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That whole attitude. Acting like I can't fuck you whenever and whatever way I want."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "That will bring a child of whose claim to power is legitimate in strength, as well as in blood."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That will give me enough votes to secure what I wanted regardless."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a stern, commanding tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That will keep him in check. Make sure he gets no ideas. So he remembers whose in charge on this ship."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a thoughtful concern
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That will likely slow us down."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That will take us into the inner palace grounds."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Angry indignation
msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That won't be enough!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly assuring
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That won't be necessary blondie."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a resigned sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That won't do."
