msgid "The Khan was quiet for a moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Khan waved his great hands."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Khan waved his hand, dismissing her further prostration."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "The Khan will come and visit you tonight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "The Khan's of the past were men of great power and great ambition. But what drove them was small."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Khan, for his part, was quick to catch on."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Harshly condemning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Khan, the man that broke her nation and made her people slaves, had made her a slave..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously excited, warmly congratulatory
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "The Khan...he is hosting a feast to celebrate our victory."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Kitchen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Knight drew his blade from its sheath, glittering with silver light."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Legions of Mythran, send by Gilead, greeted her with raised fists."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Lower-Ward, out near the docks. Not the best part of town, but far from the worst. Working people most of all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, instructively
msgctxt "speaker:Servant"
msgid "The Master awaits, please follow me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "The Master can be strict, but if you behave, he can be kind too!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "The Master didn't tell me, but why bother to serve a God that you can kill?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "The Master has a lot of appetites. I think I spend more nights with him than by myself here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "The Master is far too powerful for some Hellhounds to come and bother us."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Excitedly exclaiming
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "The Master wants us to be roommates!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly welcoming
msgctxt "speaker:Servant"
msgid "The Master will receive you. Please, enter."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a puzzled, concerned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor burried his head in his hands."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor grabbed her hands just before she left."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor looked up, his eyes bright."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor nodded, absently."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor nodded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor rolled up his sleeves and pulled the tools from the bag."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a calm, resigned sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor sighed as he finished stitching up the girl."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor stood up."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reluctantly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mayor wanted me to march my whole army through the forest. Sweep through every corner."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously worried
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mayor was murdered...strangers in the town the night before...they'll start looking around."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor's face sank."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a proud, energetic tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor's hands moved with a swift and practiced ease."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a heavy heart, solemnly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mayor's shoulders fell lower as he leaned forward."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "The Mayor...the townsfolk?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "The Miller girl? Yes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Mythran Empire is vast, and even inside of the Empire, it is divided against itself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "The Mythran Empire itself, of course."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran Prince shook his head."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mythran armies, two legions in total, will soon land on our shores."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, unenthusiastic manner
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "The Mythran army came through the main gate, as expected, but they brought more heavy artillery than we expected."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran army made no objection of slavery, given that it was the law-of-the-land back in Mythra, and so nobody stopped the mercenary company from taking their own slaves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "The Mythran camp is in a bit of chaos after their prince was...well, you know."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "The Mythran prince has entered the city and he's drawing closer to the palace."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Amusedly teasing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran prince laughed as he spoke, mocking the Shah."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran prince laughed, his voice echoing through the vast throne room."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Playfully teasing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran prince laughed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran prince moved closer towards the Shah."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran prince raised one eyebrow."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Mythran soldiers had looked on with surprise as the mercenary company had rallied the wagons and set out past the great city gates of Bagrad."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "The Mythrans acknowledge nothing but the supremacy of their own Eternal Court, but they will gladly play on our own divisions."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Eagerly hopeful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Mythrans are eager enough to gain a foothold in the Union Kingdoms that they will support your cause."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, slightly concerned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Mythrans are less restrictive, but I don't imagine everyone will be as free as you in their thinking."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Stern determination
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "The Mythrans rely on this, because they know a united Union would be too much for their two legions."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determinedly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "The Mythrans will land on our shore, unified. We must be the same."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mythrans will likely demand access, we'll deny them, they'll negotiate with Vaelen, drag it out, buy ourselves time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mythrans will not land on our shores alone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mythrans will prove no different."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "The Mythrans, the people in charge, whoever the fuck decides things like this?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly detached
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Mythrans, they are not so concerned with who comes from where. They are rather a bit more practical."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Mythrans? You do business with them?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a thoughtful, reverent tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Nexus of their faith."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Noble families that have managed to escape, largely gathered here in Rahayal."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Noctori are different from you and I."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively, with concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Northern provinces had made clear that they felt left out of the growing economy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker-name"
msgid "The Official"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Grim determination
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman grabbed her by her arm and pulled her up."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman leaned in and whispered."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman looked directly at her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly, with a hint of nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman nodded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman sighed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman smiled."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman still kept her in his grip."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Old Tribesman was the leader of the pack, likely by age. Most of the others were younger, closer to her own age."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily exhaling frustration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Orc had more than long lost his patience."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "The Orc tribes are not what they used to be. They've forgotten how to build siege weapons and such."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "The Orcs and Goblins like easy prey."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a chilling and grave tone
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "The Orcs went on a rampage. Looting, murdering, making slaves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "The Order has an obsession with the past. You have nearly as many classes related to history as you do spellcasting."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly delivering
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "The Order has left the city to its ruins, and rightly so. For millenia it was silent."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Order would be an invaluable ally against these creatures."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "The Pantheon of your Gods is a hierarchy of power. Those who sit at the top, and the many who sit at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Rosannan army had been slow to mobilize, but was by now quickly gathering."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Rosannan people were mostly farmers, dreaming of living easy lives with good harvests."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with wonderment
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "The Rose Knight...I think they're calling you..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Rose family can feel it in the air..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Bitterly mournful
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Royal Family of Rosanna is gone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously respectful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Royal Messenger bowed with the practiced grace of an experienced creature of the court, then turned and left."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Samayra opposite of her was a very different creature from the girl she knew."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflecting admiration and warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Sarah that had looked down on a man she had so barely known. The only man that ever showed her an ounce of kindness after losing everything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly disdainful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah Mahda, too arrogant to let this slight pass, killed the young Mythran prince."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly pacing back and forth
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah began to anxiously pace from side to side."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah gestured with his hand, as if the matter was settled."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah had failed to understand that Bagrad survived by virtue of being too unimportant to conquer, but with the spilling of important blood he had given a cause for war that weighed heavier than strategy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disinterestedly observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah had spoken to his daugther, but paid her little heed after, turning his attention back to Xan."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "The Shah is finally desperate enough to give us access to the hoard. All we need to do is keep him and his family safe."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Lightly chuckling and amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah laughed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly with a sense of foreboding
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah sat down in his throne and motioned for Xan and Sarah to come near."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah shook his head in disbelief."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully, with a hint of curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah shook his head."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sharp, intense anger
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah stomped the edge of his throne with his fist again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah's bluff had been called, but Xan had tactfully allowed him to withdraw with his ego in tact."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah's face turned white as paper, as if the very idea of defeat had never crossed his mind before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intensely focused, commanding respect
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah's imperious voice cut through the room, all attention centering on him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a frantic, hysterical tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah, beyond himself, laughing hysterically at the carnage."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm, with surprise
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Shah, prone to rage, appeared calmer than she had ever seen him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly recounting past events
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "The Shah...Samayra...you told them we would come back, to protect them..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ui"
msgid "The Survival of Sarah Rose"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mix of pride and excitement
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Survival of Sarah Rose is an epic fantasy game. Production on TSSR is still ongoing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively somber
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Tribes are weakened. The death of their Khan has left them divided."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribes had struck, nearly without warning."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hushed, wary tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribes were formidable warriors...she risked having come so far in all these years, only to lose to them in her most crucial hour."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman advanced one step."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly, with a sense of regret
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman behind her continued to take her, ravage her as he rode her to her climax and then kept her there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman dropped his blade as he instintively reached up, trying to pull the orc's hands from around his face."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman frowned."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a resigned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman lashed out at her, but his blade bounced off her armor."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Gently amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman laughed and shook his head."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman looked at her again, then the gathered crowd."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman looked at her, frowning."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In an urgent, menacing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman lunged, swiping at her with his curved blade."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a neutral, attentive manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman nodded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman nodded. He admitted to it as casually as if she had asked him about the weather."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman raised his glass and threw back his head, drinking with abandon."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a respectful distance, contemplatively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman sat firmly in his own saddle, eyeing her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman shook his head."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman sighed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman stared directly at her as he moved closer, all of his murderous intent aimed at her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With amused sarcasm
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman swung his blade, catching Atilla on the arm, but he had swung poorly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously troubled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman was deadly, but the ground, now turned to mud, was equally dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman's art was more graceful, spinning and twisting in ways that were only possible for someone carrying little armor."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a haunted hush, with a sinking heart
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman, silenced, his head gone, crushed between the orc's massive hands."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman, who looked on with equal surprise that their enemy had just decided to ride into the city without guards."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesman."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "The Tribesmen appreciate any slave that learns their language. And Gods know they won't learn any other language."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "The Tribesmen are all up in a small fort in the center of town."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with mild amusement
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "The Tribesmen are not a complicated people. They like a pretty girl for...well, the obvious reasons."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen army, from what she could tell by sight and from her reports, was decidely smaller than her army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily anticipating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen charge cut deep into her army's core, slaughtering soldiers with blade and stomping hooves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen continued to move towards them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen cut through them as if they were nothing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen did not share her people's aversion to nakedness, and so she had seen more naked men since she arrived here than all her life before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly conveying respect
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen did not simply value strength, it was the only principle by which they lived."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually amused
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "The Tribesmen don't know too much about farming and such."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "The Tribesmen enjoy conquering their enemies, but they also enjoy breaking them. Humiliating them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen famously did not have any navy, and the old Rosannan fleet had fled after the fall."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily conveying the futility
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen fought bravely, but their numbers had dwindled so far that they could no longer mount a proper defense."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Alertly curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen had fled the city by early hour, keeping true to their word."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen had never truly intended to rule over the land or the people. Not as genuine rulers."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a thoughtful, measured tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen had no intention of attacking directly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen had the advantage of surprise, but judging from their numbers, there weren't as many as she had first feared."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly, yet still hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen had underestimated their people, drunk on their victory."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "The Tribesmen have lost some interest in Rosanna, this is true, but they are still a warrior people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen held out a cup to the male slave."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen might be weakened, but they were still formidable warriors. She could not risk an ambush."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly with dismay
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen simply raided as they pleased."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "The Tribesmen supposedly killed their way through a good few men before they found one that was willing to bend for them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were a proud people, and some would rather die in battle than withdraw."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily recounting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were experienced in war, but sieges were something they had far less experience with."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were famous for their mastery of such strategies."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were quicker, but not by much."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously proud
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were skilled warriors."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were still deadly, inflicting a hard blow, but they were too small in numbers to win."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, nostalgic tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen were warriors, yes, but they were warriors of the land. The desert."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously escalating, with a mix of frustration and urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen's mad charge was slowing down, having lost their initial momentum and finding more bodies in their way."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen, deadly as they were, were only few in numbers compared to her own army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively recounting, with a hint of pride
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen, having had their fill of the show, returned to their food and drink."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen, hoping to catch her army by surprise by charging around the city, had left the city itself undermanned."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen, long gone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen, moving like ants across the walls of the city. The occasional scout group that dared outside."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Tribesmen, so frenzied in their chase, allowed their bloodlust to overtake reason."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly, with disdain
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "The Trickster God."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "The Union Council is an outdated system, belonging to an even more outdated era."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Union Councils appeared shortly after the collapse of the Union itself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Conveying with a tone of respectful curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "The Union Kingdoms have often proven to be a particularly difficult region of the world to gain a foothold in for the Mythrans."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense, alarmed delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Union fell into civil war."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The Union had naturally come about as the peoples of the region evolved from nomadic life to settled life."
