#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There we go, I might actually make a decent Knight after all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contentedly satisfied
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There we go, nice and steady."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, with slight disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There we go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, with slight disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "There we go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, with slight disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Jacob"
msgid "There we go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Serenely pleased
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There we go. Nice and calm."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Mildly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There we go..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Deliberately revealing, with intrigue
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There we'll find the entrance to the Labyrinth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Quietly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were a few patrons about, but nothing too busy. The sounds of the city were still here, but muted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There were a few things, like drugs, but above all, alcohol."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were a lot of rules, tricks and strategies, and Sarah had to confess she'd never really mastered the game."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with slight surprise
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were adjustments, measurements, sail rigging, but all in all, the work had dropped off considerably."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were close to twenty soldiers, each massive in size and armed with real weapons and armor."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly reciting
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There were fathers that killed sons and sons that killed fathers. Brother killing brother."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued yet wary
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were few windows, leaving the great palace feeling oddly muted in its colours, but also keeping the punishing desert heat out."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were her own soldiers from the mercenary company."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were her soldiers. Her servants. Her attendants."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There were many chains, some more obvious and some less, that weighed on those such as us."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were many women who did worse for a meal, she thought. Perhaps she wasn't so different from them as she had once imagined."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were men, women, working side by side, and Sarah even saw some other species."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were moments were she longed to be loved by him, held by him, and to hear him whisper sweet words."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flat, detached delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no animal noises."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no more questions to be settled of what came next. How she would survive. No more decisions to be made."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no more words needed between them, for Sarah felt the same."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no riches to be found, but they could make a life. Survive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily recounting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no torches, no braziers, nothing that could ward this opressive darkness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, wide-eyed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no words for the sight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Quiet resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no words that would save her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were noises outside, as there always were. Lethram was a city that rarely went truly quiet."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively considering
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were now several lines between herself and the enemy, and their progess had grinded to a halt."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly recounting a distant sight
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were only a few lights, tiny hovels each a great distance away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a thoughtful musing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were other things she could do. Train by herself. Study even more. But something kept her here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were others that could steer the ship in the armada."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were people, off in the main streets, working, shopping, but nobody noticed or cared for her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were plenty of real dangers all around her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were rules and laws in Lethram...but the city guard was not without its freedom to deal with problems in their own way."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were slave soldiers, craftsmen, sailors. There were even slave generals and slave diplomats."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily, with a hint of bitterness
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There were those I killed that deserved everything they got and more."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Coldly dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were those who build this marvel, Sarah realized, and there were those who would destroy it. She was the latter."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were times she found herself missing the security of that routine. Then there were times where Sarah loved the dynamism of this city."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Wearily disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There were times when mages tried to affect the world, but our magic, it's too strange for people. It's too unnatural."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were too many."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There were wars and conflict, but nothing crazy. Nothing like what the world looks like now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were worse ways to spend her last night on earth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly longing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There will be a day when you wish you took my hand, and when that day comes, remember that I offered, and it was you who declined."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There will be a great feast tonight. It is a rare fact to have every ruler of the Union Kingdoms under one roof."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously anticipating
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There will be hundreds of archers in that army, crossbowmen..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly, with concern
msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "There will be more attacks. More wounded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determinedly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There will be no country left to defend in the capital falls. Making our stand here, means pushing Hassar's forces back into the desert. That will help everyone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassuring, with patience
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There will be plenty of days to work on the paperwork when we travel back to Mythra. No need to get it all done tonight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There will be time, Sarah thought, for him to grow into it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm reassurance
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There will never be another attack, and in a few years, this will all just be an aweful story people tell."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily, with a hint of urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be a battle tomorrow, and she could not afford to be distracted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be a next chapter to her life, she knew this, and it was that belief that kept her alive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be a time to make a move. Eventually. But not now. She knew too little of this place, and the mark still haunted her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no answer."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With sincere admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no denying that she had enjoyed it, that much she could never deny between them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, detached tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no leader at all. A Council would rule instead."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determined resolve
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no other chance. If she wanted her freedom, she would have to seize this moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tiredly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be other times to talk to the girl, and she feared she might add more stress for no reason."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, incredulous excitement
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "There you are!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, slightly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "There you are."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There you go again. Pretending you don't want something you do want. That's what gets you all twisted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously excited
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There you go, Blondie."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There you go, just like that. A little faster."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Male Soldier"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There you go..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "There you go..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "There you go..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There you have it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a playful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There! Fits like a glove."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There's a chest over there. Go ahead and open it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There's a lot you don't know about me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There's a reason I took your little barriers apart like they were nothing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There's a restaurant nearby that I've been wanting to try."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There's a small chapel in Northam. Overlooking the sea."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There's a spot over here, in the grass."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "There's a tent here!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There's only one question. Do you feel better?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There's some resentment there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tentatively probing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There's something wrong."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There's the real you, Blondie."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Excitedly welcoming
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "There's the wench!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a teasing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "There, I think you got me good and started."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively somber
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, Sarah sat and wept, until after much time, her senses returned to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With cautious anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, a black monolith waited for her, and whispered."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, around the campfire, she saw the others."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a startled, incredulous gasp
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, as she had already suspected, she found not her usual shape, but instead a man's one."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively listening
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, as the celebration proceeded without them, Sarah sat and listened as Kate held her own eulogy for him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, as they approached the gate of Calshure, Sarah saw an odd thing happen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally factual
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, at the back, were mostly archers and lightly armored footmen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In awe, with reverence
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, atop the steps, the throne loomed large."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "There, go read that. Maybe that will clear out your mind."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, hidden, safe from the world, lost to their love."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued yet cautious
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There, holy man. How about you go count these outside for a bit?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, in her bed, Sarah couldn't help but find herself staring at Samayra's body."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, in the distance, was the city square atop which they had constructed their camp."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, in the midsts of the small clearing in front of the tent, Sarah found her friend."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, it skips from thirty-eight to forty. What about pot number thirty-nine?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, looking back at her, his perfect smile."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There, looking like a princess again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Comforting, reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, now don't be too sad, alright?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, on the far side of the throne room, cowering behind the throne, Sarah could see Samayra."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly exhausted
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, on the table, she remained exhausted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, re-throw those."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Caringly concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There, rest. You are spend."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, she saw him stirring again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, somewhere in the third week or so, Hugh appeared at their door as he had many times before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a dismissive tone
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "There, take a seat over there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contentedly satisfied
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "There, that should be enough of that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There, the Three Sisters held court, and held sway over life and death."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly apprehensive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, the black violation of natural space, still loomed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, the two women, distant as they were, finished together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly, lovingly
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There, there dear."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Hushed, reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There, there..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Hushed, reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There, there..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm reassurance
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "There, trapped, the darkness reached out and spoke to me, but it did not frighten me, Sarah, rather, it soothed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "There, try this one."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, wailing to herself, Sarah was come upon by Kate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There, we can set up tonight's camp there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a serene, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, with hands entwined, the two women lost themselves to the madness of their moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "There."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There. It is done."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Shah Mahda"
msgid "There. Those are the directions to the vault. Take them, if you promise you will negotiate our surrender and keep my daughter safe."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There...were bandits there?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These Noctori live long lives, but only in so far as that they are granted this longevity by this source of power."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These Noctori...they are all quite selfish in the end."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "These Tribesmen are good warriors, but they're not that good."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These Woodland spirits...they see the world in troubled ways. Like looking through a fogged window."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously intoning
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "These alleys and streets are dangerous. You'd be better off stayin with me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are all the servants?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These are called Voidrifts. They're wounds upon reality."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are his private quarters?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, slightly awestruck
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "These are rare artifacts, called fate stones."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Narrow-eyed, with suspicion
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These are the books that will make some, and break others. These numbers determine who gets to live in the big houses and who gets to live in the small ones."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Officer"
msgid "These are the current drafts of our defensive lives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These are the known places where we've had attacks. About a doze or so now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are your...?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with a hint of surprise
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These creatures from the void were unlike anything she'd ever known."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These dark corners of the world, where the people of lowest character dwelled."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "These days she lives out on our family estate. Tending the gardens."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively considering
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These days, if I'm on the road for more than a week, I can feel it in my bones."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Beneath a veneer of casual indifference
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These drunkards, who likely had drank away the last of their coin, were now above her. Using her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "These extreme times call for extreme measures, and so with a heavy heart I will take on myself the title of old."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These four countries together covered most of the Northern side of the great ocean, flanked only by the great desert to the east and the Hyral mountains to the west."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These gardens..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These had come to the men of the march once as curses, now as treasured possessions to the mad few that continued to march."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively explaining
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These here are all the legal work we need to get sorted before we get to Mythra."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally observing
msgctxt "speaker:Elsa"
msgid "These here are the menu items."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These last few days out here have been nice, but my life is a lot busier than you might think. Usually."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These men and women, millenia old, who walked a world so different from theirs..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly informative
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "These men hail from the Northern province, where they worked as merchants."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With deep respect and solemnity
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These men made a vow and they kept it, even if it meant giving up their lives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These men were dressed for battle, as best as poor men could be."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Noddingly approving
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These men, all these men, desired her. And if she learned to trade herself for the proper price, she could make something out of nothing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective tone, with slight apprehension
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These mountains, dangerous and inhospitable, could not support large armies in the way the open plains could."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "These orc mountains, only orcs live here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a playful and teasing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These particular ones could be cultivated into a potion that would harden the skin, so much so that swords would bounce off it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These parts of town were dangerous, but with a small magical flame for light, Sarah managed to find her way and kept anyone from bothering her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "These people are alive because of you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, with concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These people, safe, feared the arrival of so many fleeing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These places and the people here, they didn't matter to the historians that wrote the large tomes that detailed the lives of Kings and Queens."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These places lived in a perpetual shade, Sarah realized as she followed Alaric."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly, with a hint of anger
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These prices, I can't work with them, I'll go find a real merchant with a real price."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detachedly indifferent
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "These proposals, I frankly don't care much for one way or the other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a sharp, sarcastic tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "These ropes are fine as they are blondie, how about you go and wash the linnens."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contentedly embracing the scars
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "These scars I'll bear gladly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a dismissive, condescending tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "These shadow things? Someone more important than me can decide what needs to be done there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly, with sorrowful resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These shadowy creatures ripped and murdered for seemingly no reason at all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Barion"
msgid "These soldiers will take you back to your room until further order."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, attentively
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These things represent the ripping of that fabric."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These things...nobody gets it right the first time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with fascination
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These totems will distract the Woodland spirits. For a while at least."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a frustrated, angry tone
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "These troublemakers then! They are blocking the road!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Bitterly disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "These tunnels can be a bitch if you get lost."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These tunnels will take us deeper into the labyrinth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These two men, each in their prime, their naked bodies pressing against each other..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Pensively introspective
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "These unresolved questions...they are a weakness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were all her peers. None were obliged to show her the curtesy that most other commoners and nobles alike owed her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were all the Tribesmen had brought to her people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtful curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were heads, but judging by their features, they were clearly Tribesmen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously anticipating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were men with pent up urges, and they had found in her a willing release for it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were the moments where she wished she could just stay in forever."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were the only words she could muster."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly, tenderly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were the only words she managed to produce, quiet as a mouse."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly with a touch of awe
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "These women are fine and proper royal ladies of the court of Bagrad."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly respectful
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "These women here, my fine friends, aren't just any ladies."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a sense of wonder and calm delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These words seemed to calm Samayra down."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly, with resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They advanced...but not really."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low, ominous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "They ain't gonna let you die, but they won't lose a night sleep over you not eatin for a day either."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued and amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They all passed through the castle, some so trivial they made Sarah want to scream out and remind everyone they were at war."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised realization
msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They all said the stone was black, but it seemed so obvious that it was red."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They all suffered their ends."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They all take place outside the village."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They all went quiet as they listened to him speak, loudly, boasting, in his Tribal tongue."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They allow masters to set their slaves free, but they are no fools."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They also said it was the most advanced form of magic, and that only the greatest mages could master it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, slightly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They always do, sooner or later."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They always say that, don't they?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They applied a red paint to her body, painting ritual markings that made no sense to her but seemed sacred to them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Coldly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are as weak husbands, demanding a reward because they were faithful to their wives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They are collected. Put to work. Returned."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They are creatures of the void, born out of the shadows in the under realm."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "They are disciplined, strong, experienced."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Inquisitively skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are dressed little different than farmers. Merchants. Tell me how I know these to be bandits and not victims?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are driven by a simple desire, to escape their horrid torture. And for a brief moment, they will. But they are lured into a trap. A war they cannot win."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "They are instead grown by combining the basics of growing plants, with magical infusion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are looking for something, buried in the sands of the city. Something they have been searching for, for a long time now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are loyal to us, as the lesser lords are loyal to them, and as the peasants are loyal to them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They are members of the Highfield family."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are more often a simple kind, with simple pleasures."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are my friends, my family. Not by blood, but by choice."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly admiring, with warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Emmissary"
msgid "They are my gift to you, Princess of Rosanna."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With pride and exuberance
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are my people!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly convinced
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are not the way of the world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They are the leaders of the Mythran Empire, yes, but they are in their own way enslaved."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With reverent admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are the well from which all the laws that govern nature spring forth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly exhausted
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are tired, spend. Our supplies dwindle."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a confident, reassuring tone
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They are trying to kill you, but they will not succeed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They are! Here, follow me and I'll take you there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly recounting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They argued back and forth for a while."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They assigned us to work the same shift."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily narrating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They ate and shared stories until deep into the night, until it had become so late they were forced to go home."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They awoke early the next day to continue their exploration of the forest."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anticipating rebellion
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They balanced on a riot. Mutiny."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They been spreading that story before I was even a kid."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began in the bed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to pull and move her body like a ragdoll."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to pull her away with such strength that she could not offer any resistance."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to speak to one another in a foul language she had no way of understanding."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a grave, ominous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They began to teach their followers how to wield God killing magic as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, wide-eyed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to throw their magics at it, whipping the beast into a furious frenzy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly recounting with intrigue
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to walk together, down one of the hallways, away from the celebrating masses."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to walk, crossing the vast Receiving Hall and entering the palace interior."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, matter-of-fact tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They begin to drag the men away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Noddingly impressed
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They believe that they are entitled to the women they conquer, because they are the strongest."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly supportive
msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "They believe that together, one highly trained male soldier and female soldier, can make one perfectly rounded warrior."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily suspicious
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They believed that with you and your brother under arrest, they could take over the country with little bloodshed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Carefully observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They belonged to Sarah alone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They block the sight of the gods, making them blind to what transpires near the stone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, detached manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They blocked their path."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They bore witness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They both look at captain Belmont and yell out in unison."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They both saw the future, and uttered it into existence, at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They both walked towards the fire, as if drawn by instinct."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly recounting with solemn respect
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They broke the great Orc Hordes of old, crushing them on the open fields and chasing them into the mountains where they now lived in squalor."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, pleading tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They broke the spirit of the people of Calshure, over and over again, praying for one of them to rise up and be a worthy fight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously curious
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They broke through..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low, mysterious whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They brought up all the girls and they forced them to look at the stone and tell him what it looked like."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They call it Martial Arts. It's a special form of fighting in the Far Lands."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They call me Raza. What is your name?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised yet amused
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They call me a military prodigy, but I don't know about all that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They came in all shapes, sizes and ages."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Frustrated indignation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They can all go to hell if they think they get to tell me anything today."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Urgently concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They can cross the distance between the eastern district and the capital much faster than a regular army could. They could cut off the capital in a matter of days."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They can do the grunt work of ripping open drawers, hoping to find a necklace. Gods know I did that shit long enough."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They can even vary by the very laws that govern them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective wonderment
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "They can sense other creatures floating in that space."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They can't expect us to agree to that...can they?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detachedly, with slight annoyance
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They can't respect rank."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They can't survive in our world for very long. It will rage for a few days, then slowly collapse and die."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a subdued, serious tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "They captured him, his wife, his four sons and two daughters."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disinterestedly dismissing others
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They cared nothing for those who ended up here. Much less for the Arts that the Imperial family pursued."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a hint of playful sarcasm
msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They catch you or buy you?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They caught her staring."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They caught me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemnly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "They celebrate the year passing same time each year. Each time, I put a notch in the beam there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With growing excitement
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They chanted her name, and with each chant, her name grew louder."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They clanked their chalices together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, detached manner
msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They come and go."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They come in all kinds of shapes, and I'll admit, this one was bigger than the usual kind."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Condescendingly scoffing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They consider loot earned without bloodshed to be...dishonorable."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly with satisfaction
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued along the road for several more days, before finally coming upon the village of Hillstown."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued their screams as she looked out over them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued to explore the festival ground together whilst eating."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued to play the game. Round afte round."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively, with a sense of wonder
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued to walk through the vast, almost endless, gardens of the palace."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued walking."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a concerned whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could be broken."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could be dangerous, but there was a reason for why they acted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could hardly keep a bonfire going. The days of their glory had long faded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could have all shouldered a great deal, knowing that their trials might soon end, but by now, nobody could be certain if they would ever end at all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could manage a night without her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determinedly urging action
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could not just sit here and wait for the Tribesmen to finish them off."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They could reach back and resume all the injustices that had slipped by in their absence."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Enigmatically intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could speak without words."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "They crawl on their knees but they don't pull up their skirts properly, so they usually scrape them and tear them on a loose brick."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a warm, hopeful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They crawl through the frenzy and find one another. Their hands link. Neither fears death as it comes for them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, excitedly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cried out her name, louder and louder."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cried out their loyalty all at once."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a weary, exhausted manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cross the vast throne room, each near exhaustion as they finally get back to the exit that Xan had made."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a resigned sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cursed many things, but as men are prone to do, they soon found a concensus for their hatreds."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly reciting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cut him down, but he was already cold to the touch, long dead."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a cold, skeptical tone
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They deeply believe in the system of slavery, and so anything done to overturn that is looked upon with suspicion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They delighted in knowing the pain they inflicted on them, each time another girl was married off to a tribesmen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly informative
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They deliver most of our coal and iron."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pensive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They desired a lifetime but had only a night to themselves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They desired only that we made use of it for as long as we pleased, and when we were finished with life, we could go to the tower of dying, and fade away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Bitterly disappointed, yet quietly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They did as they were told, but a cold rage was growing in them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Angry indignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They did not eat as animals did. Nor did they conquer as men did. They simply destroyed anything and everything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemnly disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Advisor"
msgid "They did not even care for a meeting."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They did not know war, and so they did not fear it the way they should."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't care enough to stop her. Nor enough to help."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disgustingly annoyed
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They didn't give a fuck, so they simply constructed these large housing blocks."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They didn't have one in your size, so they had to make that one custom."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They didn't let me in the church, obviously, but I got to watch from my little room how he walked in there with all the others."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't need words, Sarah thought to herself as she fell back into the bed, pulling the girl with her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't seem intent on meeting the Rosannan army on the open field, but rather, to agitate them to attack first."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't want to be here, and the desert didn't want them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Dispassionately neutral
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They died without in great numbers and with little glory."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They discuss strategy, organizing local militias to resist the raiding party, deploying additional scouts."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "They dissapear."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They do?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a confident, authoritative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They dominate the beginning and the end."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a disappointed sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They don't deserve this...she doesn't deserve this..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently and encouragingly
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They don't force you or anything. You can just work the shift."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mixture of relief and curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They don't see much of the captain after that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective tone, with slight sadness
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They don't understand the culture, how we fight among one another but still remain suspect of outsiders."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a calm, reassuring tone
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They don't worry about hurting you. They worry about hurting his pride."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disdainfully condescending
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They don't. They think you are weak. Vulnerable."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised exclamation
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They don'ts know how to be proper round a lady, too long out at sea pokin each other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptically intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They doubted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They drag her out of the auction house, through the busy streets, and down alleys."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a haunting sadness
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They dream of a violent death."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They dresses were made of a fine silk, a rich embroidery decorating from the waist down to the skirt line."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They drew their cloaks as tight around themselves as they could manage."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Indifferently amused
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They drink, they feast, and that seems to be about all they do."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each held a branch of dreamstalk in their hands, as if it were made of gold."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively, with a sense of nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each retired to their own bedroll."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each sat down again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Inspiring, hopeful delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each took one step and crossed a million."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a tender, loving embrace
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They embrace each other, the captain's cum still on them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a concerned, investigative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They ended up in a decidedly poorer part of town. Boarded up windows, drunkards, trash heaped up."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They ended up looting the wrong city near one of the borders."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They enjoyed, more than anything, the dominance of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a mocking tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They expect it because they were fools and did not know the law of their new land."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively curious
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They extend from here, all the way up north to the mountains, and around there, they turn into swamplands."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Conveying a tone of deep regret and profound sadness
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They failed to see the world for what it was, and so instead they fell into despair."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Gravely concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Ragged Man"
msgid "They fear what all parents fear, to lose sight of their child. They urge you to turn away from this path to nothingness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly disgusted
msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They feast. All drunk. Stupid!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, emotionless delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They featured blackmail, bribery and at times even assassinations."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With somber resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fell to the earth, their bodies mixed in with the mud and snow and blood."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They felt like treason to her own ears."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They finally arive in Lethram."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They finally broke through the thick forest, coming back out on the open road."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Gently content, with satisfaction
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They finished their meal together, chatting away the hours until night came."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They fled beyond the borders of this world, hiding themselves in a space that even they themselves are blind to."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somber reflection
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They forgettin there's all sorts of worlds out there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, with slight curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They form the council that send people out on missions. They're the ones that send me off to the ruins, in fact."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fought among each other. They carried out the occasional raid when they dared."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fought not with knightly skill, but pure and raw strength."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hushed, intense battle cry
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "They fought the Voidlings and their three-sister demons to a stalemate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They found the creature, and fearing for its life still, it threw itself on their mercy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly stating facts
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fucked themselves into exhaustion, the sweat dripping from their bodies, only adding to the overwhelming sensations."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, dispassionate manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fucked until their bodies could carry them no further, and each sank and collapsed into an oblivion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gathered in the council room of the castle."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gathered up their plates and headed inside."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gesture and yell, towards her, towards them. Nobody speaks the language, but everyone understands."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hesitant
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They get hard to count after a while."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They get paid, sure, and if they survive they'll win some glory, but for the most part it leaves the economies of these small towns in shambles."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Annoyingly dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They go around telling you what you can and can't do so much you start to believe it. But they have no right."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sardonically amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gossiped about them. Insulted them. Laughed at them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a neutral, informative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "They got some, but they're still pouring it. Said it will be a few minutes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They grab the leader first."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They grew up in the same town, and after it was burned down in a raid, decided to stick together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They had a whole civilization here...long before any other came along."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a sudden excited rush
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had barely closed the door before they were all over each other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had become only painful reminders of what she had lost."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been friends a lifetime ago, and it struck Sarah as remarkable that they had somehow found one another again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been loyal."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a neutral, observant tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been marching for a long day."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a troubled, concerned whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been out there until their father had furiously come to collect them, warning them of the cold."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly resolved
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been ready to die. Every Tribesman was trained to expect death."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With sincere admiration and a hint of warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been right. She wouldn't have survived for a day out here without them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly satisfied
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been saved."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been searching for an odd, defenseless girl. None of them had signed up to fight a mage."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been some of the first to embrace her in the mercenary company."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been through a lot together, survived one battle after the other, and still Sarah worried the same each time for Kate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been together for little more than a month, a fleeting moment across the whole of her life, and still that fraction of her life loomed larger than most others."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been trained to deal with pickpockets and other lowlives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been trained to fight in battles against other soldiers, few knew anything about magic, other than to run away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hopeful, yet somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had believed in victory, but now they had a taste of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful, then resigned defeat
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had believed in victory, but now they had tasted defeat."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly realizing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had clearly been wrong on the latter, Sarah thought."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Optimistically confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had conquered a great city, were rich on loot. They had a reason for being in good spirits."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptically intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had considered buying a new one, but they could not have justified the price."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had continued to make good distance in the days that followed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had crowded around a young man with a thin frame and long, flowing blonde hair, reaching to his shoulders."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised gasp
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had cut so deep into her army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, slightly disappointed tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had defeated the Tribes, but victory was not so clean."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had developped into quite a team over the few days spend together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, monotonous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had discussed strategy, he had offered some words of comfort, but in the end there wasn't much else he could offer."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had done many things together in their short time, violating the law and each other. Yet despite all these things, Sarah had kept a great part of herself hidden."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With cautious optimism, attentively
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had driven her out as a foolish girl, but she would return to them a warrior."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflecting warmth, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had each other, and it was all they needed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Delicate curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had exchanged glances, kisses and touches. Still this felt more intimate than any of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had explored every corner of the castle together, for years, they had been inseparable."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had feared the Tribesmen, as well they should have, but now they learned they were as mortal as any other man."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemnly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had gambled a lot on the hope that they might kill her and break apart her army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had gathered in a wide circle around her, and in their midsts, Samayra performed as only she could."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With hopeful anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had hoped this would be the case."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously uneasy
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They had it empty for a while after the last girl decided to run away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With careful tenderness
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had just scrapped the frost off one of the rigging chains and despite wearing gloves, each of their hands were swollen and red from the cold."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They had kept their plans well hidden, but Barion saw me as a friend, and he confided in me shortly before the meeting began."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had kissed before, but this...this time it was different."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had left her a shabby blanket as a cloak, or perhaps, to cover herself up in hopes not to look at her anymore."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had left the city, Sarah realized only now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had looked on with even greater surprise when they saw the mercenaries leave, not through the western gates for Lethram, but the long abandoned eastern gates to nowhere."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly, with resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made a fool out of her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made camp deep in the forest."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hopeful yet concerned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made good progress and she had seen few if any signs of bandits."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sorrowfully lamenting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made her a slave."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had managed Marius, but what had she won, truly?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had marched from the capital straight towards the province of Dianthus, home of the Achillea family and center of the rebellion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Patiently curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had marched on longer than usual, making up time by pushing themselves to keep going through the first hours of the night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had met for a moment when the old soldier pulled on the chain and dragged her through a door, off to the back of the auction house. Wherever it was he wanted to go, he seemed to be in a hurry."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily cautious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had nearly lost everything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had never dared to speak of what their relationship was, but Sarah knew it had gone too far many times."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Deliberately calm, almost reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had never spoken of it explicitly, but Sarah was no fool to the reality of life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised realization
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had not been expecting to have to do any real work tonight, that much was clear to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously apprehensive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had not expected this enemy. But they had also not expected that an attack could happen everywhere all at once."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had once been so organized, so efficient."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had only just entered when he lifted her up form the ground with his arms."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised shock
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had only just stumbled inside when Sarah could feel both pair of hands on her body."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had planned to use one of the main roads from the coast to the capital to transport their army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had practiced a degree of restraint, her husband choosing to finish outside of her most evenings."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had prepared, but would it be enough?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disapprovingly disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had pretended to defend it from the walls, only to sneak out of the city from the other side, and flank them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had sat her down somewhere, but nobody told her anything. There was only the darkness."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had seemed no less real."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had set themselves towards her like a project."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had shown kindness to her when she first came to the camp."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously observant, with a hint of pride
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had spend a lifetime perfecting the sideway glance. To see without seeing. Notice without being noticed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had spend the last few years learning to listen obediently, or suffer the consequences."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, factual manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had suffered only a few casualties, and inflicted a hundred times over what they had suffered."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pensive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived the fall of Lethram. Survived their torturous journey. Land."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived the raids by the Tribesmen. They had survived the merciless frost. And now, she was rewarded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised relief
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised and hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived. They would survive longer."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With tired amusement
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had talked so long that night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had taught her a lesson. Now she would return the favor and teach the Tribes her lessons of war."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tentatively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had their torches, but she was standing in the darkness. They missed her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determinedly, with conviction
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to be decisive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a rush, concerned, subtly admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to make time, but Sarah also knew that the city and its many tall buildings offered countless chances of an ambush."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to, Sarah realized, because the harbor was filled with more ships than she had ever seen in her life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to, Sarah realized, if only to preserve the books."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had weighed on Sarah's mind all day."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They had wine or beer, so I went for wine."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a proud, celebratory tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had won."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had, quite a lot of it in fact. But most it had revolved around the union kingdoms and Rosanna itself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a cold, detached manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hate her. In her they see the cause of their circumstance. They see in her the reason for why they and their families have been made so low."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly whispering
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They hate our Order. Always have. Why, I don't know."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hated him, she saw that in their eyes, but she also knew none of them would put a stop to his."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hated their new masters still, but they hated their own men more."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Dispassionately recounting a tragic scene
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hated them for how they allowed all of this to happen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They have brought her to one of the communal slave tents, and befor her, the masses of her people are huddled up."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They have failed, at the very least to seize me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They have found no trace of Thomas..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Commandingly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "They have grown up on victory and conquest and known nothing of defeat."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a touch of melancholy
msgctxt "speaker:Ragged Man"
msgid "They have lost sight of you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, with slight surprise
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "They have money. That is not the same as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They have no interest in sharing their spoils with those conquered, so the men are fixed with these belts to keep them in line."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hesitant
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They have to sneak about and be quiet, speak in hushed tones. And each time they do, they remind everyone of where they truly stand."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They haven't done so yet?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They haven't received a shipment since these reports started. They tell me that this has never happened before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With warm curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They heaped up around her feet and not before long, she was standing naked in the tent, same as Lady Carolyn."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly resigned, with a hint of despair
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They hid away in a void beyond where anyone could reach them. A place from which they themselves did not even know to return."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They hide in the place beyond, observing the passing of this world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hold a trial, so much a mockery that it cannot even be called that in jest."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reluctantly accepting
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They hold back my head and pour more drink down my throat than I've ever gotten down before or after."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective tone, almost disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They honored her command, but Sarah could see she had lost some of their respect."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a defiant, mocking tone
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They hope to threaten each of us, and in turn, hope that one of us will strike a bargain with them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a stern, disapproving tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hurled insults at them, taunted them with stories of how much greater the tribesmen were than them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They identify, correctly, that the Union Kingdoms are fragmented and easily turned against one another."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, encouraging smile
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They initially joined the line, awaiting their turn, but upon being noticed, Hassar stood up and waived for them to advance ahead of the line."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They insisted they eat more food, and out of obligation, all of them did."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They joked among themselves, rather to share one tribesmen than be left with a Rosannan man all to yourself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Patiently optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They kept living as if they would return home to their holdings in a few months."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, detached delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept locked to their own keeps, having little interest in the people outside of what they could extract from them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a resigned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They kept telling him to sue for peace. Strike a settlement with Mythra...but he just wouldn't listen..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, curious observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept the hood over her head for long enough that Sarah began to doubt what time it was."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, watchful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept their watch, but for the rest of the night, no attack came."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept walking along the hallway."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Coldly indifferent
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They killed him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tenderly, with fondness
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kissed again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly, tenderly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kissed in between the words."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently assured
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They knew better than anyone their own strengths."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They knew it as surely as they knew all others things."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective tone, with mild surprise
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They knew that for the most part, their poverty protected them from any real looting."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Authoritatively confident
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "They knew the path that would lead to a final victory."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reluctantly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They knew they couldn't really attack her, and so they didn't."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They knew they had to wait here, to gather up all our strength before pressing into the palace."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively, with slight admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "They know the seasons as well as anyone by now. It's possible that they've adapted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They know what she is, and you know the laws."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They laid beneath the calming shade of the oak tree for so long that Sarah could hardly recall the passing of time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They laid the foundations for the world to shape itself in the only way that it ever could."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a cold, detached delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They lashed out and killed many of the rival Gods."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Playfully mocking
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They laugh, and they insult, and they make their jokes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Amused, with a hint of irony
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They laughed, not just for her situation, but they laughed because they felt relieved about how they viewed the world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly, with reverence
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They learned to weave, with approval of the Gods, their Divine nature into all manners of creations."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly, defiantly
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "They left me and my brothers and sisters behind in the capital to face a punishment for their crimes, but we are innocent."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They left me there, satisfied that by now whatever had been growing in me was surely dead."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They left."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Delicately tender
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They let the heat from their passions fade as they lay in each others arms."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They lifted her up, positioned her, then continued fucking."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They like to pretend that it has never been conquered since it was first built, but that's not true."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They like to pretend that it has never been conquered since it was first constructed, but that's not true."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly recounting, with disdain
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "They like to raid, capture strays and attack merchant caravans."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing, with slight concern
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "They like to test new girls, so be on your guard."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They listened as it slowly warmed, until finally, the water boiled."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They lived and breathed in a world of pointless cruelty and oppression, it was their oxygen."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They look towards her with panic, the way slaves perceive all new things as a source of danger."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a mix of reverence and wonder
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked at her with an odd mix of fear and gratitude."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked at her with hungry eyes, desperate for what she would give them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked at her, those blessed few, as though she had gone mad, and they feared seeing their beloved commander lost to madness. For if she could break, how did they stand any chance?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked on with dispassionate interest. They cared little for the Union Kingdoms, but they cared for a spectacle."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
