#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They watched as the soldiers rode off along different roads, gathering up everyone that lived in the town."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In an amused, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They ways of their war, swift and quick cuts, bounced harmlessly from the Knights heavy steel."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weighed heavy to the touch, a promise of what he was going to release."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They went about a corner, up a series of stairs, and then the Headmaster pushed open a door."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They went over her success with some of the seedlings. Where she had gone right. Where she had gone wrong."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral, contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were a family in the North, but only one of many and far from the most important."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were a man and a woman. The rest, illusion, meant to distract from the simple truths of nature."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were a practical people, and so they reduced the bodies of their people in equal practicality."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were all back."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily neutral
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were all going to die."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were all here for her, Sarah realized."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a concerned and urgent tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were already running dangerously low on medical supplies, just to deal with those currently wounded."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with slight surprise
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were as much on the menu as anything they brought out on a platter."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly assuring, with patience
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were asked to explain what had happened, and so they told them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Adoringly impressed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were beyond words."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They were born human, but they have undergone a transformation."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tinge of disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were certainly not a great house."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously anticipating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were children, and she did not have the heart to even hurt one hair on their heads, let alone keep them as hostages."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a solemn, concerned whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were close to the wall now. Sarah said a silent prayer that there had been no archers."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with a hint of irony
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were clothes, technically."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were coming. Her hopes of getting through the day without any violence were over."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were conquerors. They had no desire to become a part of the lands they ruled over."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were could be alone more, people raised fewer questions and rumors, and they found more opportunities to be together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily, as if revealing a dark secret
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were cruel men...but men still."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a sorrowful lament
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They were done the moment they picked up their weapons."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were dragged out by start of day for work and brought back most evenings."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With eager anticipation, with enthusiasm
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were eager for the fight, and more than that, they were even eager for a good death."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were everywhere."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were friends, but before that, she was a ruler and Kate a servant."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They were going to...they said they would..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They were gonna be visitin me at my home today."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In awe and bemusement
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were greeted with a mixture of surprise and bemusement."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were handsome enough. Crude, but that was to be expected of soldiers."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously waiting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were hardly more than a few steps in when the Tribesmen began their attack."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disapprovingly skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were having sex."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly reciting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were her people still."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were looking at them, in awe and worry."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were lucky. The crowd could have swamped them, but nobody did. Everyone decided not to get involved, letting them storm out the marketplace."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued yet distant
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They were made from a mixture of magic and metal, though the exact technique has long been lost."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a weary, exhausted sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were made to work until their hands broke, and then others would take their place."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In an admiring, slightly impressed tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were more clever than she gave them credit for. They might have laid out traps, hoping that she would rush blindly after them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were more organized than she had first assumed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were mostly City Guards, forced to fight. Their aim was poor, either by lack of practice or because they didn't want to fight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Inquisitively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were moving towards Rahayal, and all that the city promised."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Quietly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were nearing the half point, or so Belmont had told her, of what was supposed to be a two week long trip."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were no strangers so guards chasing people, but none of them had ever seen them give chase to a proper rich girl before."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently with a hint of doubt
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not at full strength."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not born into war."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously wary
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not build to welcome trade from the outside. They were build to resist the only thing Lethram expected from the hinterlands, an attack."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They were not false memories at all. They were simply the memories of others from my race. Bleeding into me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not filled with rage, or hatred or any beliefs that could be opposed."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Triumphant determination
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not going to wait out their fate inside of the city walls. They had come to meet them on the battlefield."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Earnestly committed
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They were not loyal because they stood to make money from it. They were loyal because their oathsworn duty commanded it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not men of politics or rule. They were warrior with nothing left to conquer."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not real."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, with bewilderment
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They were not so fortunate."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously uncertain
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not sure they would wake up again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hushed, ominous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were on the edge of the world, with an army that seemed on the edge of rebellion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were only a day away from the town."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were only beginning to form their relationship, and Sarah was careful not to end up as the weaker party."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were out on the edge of the world, with little more than a campfire for heat, and yet, Sarah couldn't help but feel grateful."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were ready for everything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were safe, and still they were eager for the certainty of solid ground under their feet."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were safe."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, distant gaze
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were sitting off to the side of the ship, looking out over the dock."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They were slow, just once, and it cost them their lives."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised, with concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were small infractions, and in truth, given their condition after the march in the desert, Sarah would have let it slide."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were soldiers, that much was obvious, but they also seemed...young. No older than Sarah, she estimated."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were soldiers. Inflicting wounds was easy to them. Fixing wounds was a more delicate skill."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, wistful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were stalling for time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were standing in front of a door. It didn't have any markings that made it stand out from any of the others."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were standing in pairs."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were strong, but not beyond killing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptically amused
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They were sure in the way the Gods are always sure."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low mocking tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were taunting him, kicking him."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were the kind you would expect on the ground where a door had swung open again and again, slowly leaving scratches in the floor."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They were the only ones who understood, really understood, that strength was the only power that mattered in this new age."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Heartfelt pride
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were the true heart of her nation. The people that she was tasking with ruling."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Alertly anxious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were trapped."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were trying to bleed her army out."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, accusing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were trying to overthrow her family."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were, for the most part, farmers and craftsmen, called away from their work by their lords."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a nostalgic sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weren't alone on the ship anymore, and yet she had screamed as loudly as she always did, as she had always felt."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weren't orcs...humans...but those could be equally dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weren't planning on defeating her army at all, they simply hoped to kill her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They will bring him to one of their forts, surrounded by soldiers loyal to their noble houses."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hushed, ominous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They will descend on the world like locusts and leave empires barren as fields."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly, with respect
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They will die good deaths."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admirably respectful, with a hint of pride
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They will distribute what has been conquered among those according to their rank."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a solemn, reverent tone
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They will forever remember that you sacrificed their safety, to guarantee your own."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They will humiliate you. Rosanna. Your people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With resigned apathy
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They will land on our shores and pick us off one by one. Each of us will retreat behind our walls, and we will let the others to themselves."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a hint of urgency and concern
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They will miss it, trust me on that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily anticipating
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They will not be as ready as they perhaps could have been, but they'll be as ready as we can make them, before our window closes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly assuring
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They will save you in a moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determinedly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They will seek it out, even if they lose."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They will tell stories..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They will tell tales that will move the Empire. Not instantly, but slowly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They will what?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, sorrowful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They will write history books of the evil that you did. Your family will become synonymous with treason and murder."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They will! Someone saw her through the window. They saw you walk the streets with her. People aren't fools, Jaeid."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They will, but the Mythran empire is always occupied in one place or another."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They won't do the same as part of a faceless army that holds no true allegiance to anyone other than an abstract Union."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somber resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They won't have to divide us. We're already divided."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a skeptical tone
msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "They won't try anything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In an exhausted, yet hopeful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They worked the ship deep into the night when they were called back to the captain's cabin as they always were at the end of a shift."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They worried Xan, because of their longevity, which seemed to function without any use of magic."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively with awe and respect
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They worshipped a pantheon of gods, and the rulers of this civilization could speak to them directly, as easily as you or I can speak to each other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Emotionally expressive with reverence. Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They worshipped him with their bodies. Cried out in pleasure as though it was as hymn. Screamed out his name as though the spirit was their god."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a low, ominous whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would be devoured."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would be here soon."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would be veterans soon enough, Sarah thought."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily, as if expecting danger
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would break any cavalry charge."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cheerfully singing, with celebratory excitement
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would charge into battle with song and drink themselves into a stupor to celebrate after."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would clear the distance between their armies in no time at all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would die."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would either be dragged along the current or drown. And the empire did not particularly care either way."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would fire off their arrows from a safe distance, and on their horses, chasing them on foot would be pointless."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would get to Rahayal in a few days, and then she would make her next move."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have been well on their way to Lethram by now. Sitting on a pile of gold, getting fat on good food instead of rationing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They would have even used their legions, had they not been tied down in other engagements."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously wary
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They would have killed me as gladly as I would have killed them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively with concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have to conceive. The sooner the better."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have to set out soon."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Determined, resolute
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have to travel inwards, up through the Hyral mountains. A tough journey, even when prepared. And they were not prepared."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Focused attention
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would keep running, throw away their armor, their weapons, run back to their homes and pretend to be citizens."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anticipating with eagerness
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would know she was coming. Whatever this would prove to be, it had been set in motion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a confident, knowing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They would know that I came from Rosanna. They would know of you. And they would sooner put the two together."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would know the most recent information."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would know."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would land on their shores. Very soon."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would live."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously confident
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would need a strong leader, she knew that much, but out of all them she had the least experience."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Dispassionately stating
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would never fight for her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm satisfaction
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would rest later, she figured."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a hopeful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would see her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously amused
msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "They would send in a legion, kill enough of them to send a message, then retreat."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflecting pride and admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "They would train for hours, but I'd train for days."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would warn the others that there was a girl in the ruins, not to be messed with."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They wouldn't have sounded the horns if there hadn't been danger."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber tone, conveying disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They wouldn't help her here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They yelled instructions at her, sometimes in orcish, sometimes in a broken human language."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously panicked
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They yelled, screamed, ran."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly knowing, with resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd be back, sooner or later, this much Sarah knew, but for the moment, he was spend, as was she."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly with a hint of nostalgia
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They'd bring me books and trinkets from every corner of the world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously curious
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They'd find my body dressed in military rags and ugly shoes?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd have to camp out, no matter way. Wait for next morning."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd likely call her insane, gone mad, and perhaps rightly so, she thought."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd return, they were promised, but few believed so."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Alarmingly shocked and horrified
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They'll be left to the slaughter!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With growing concern
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They'll come for us, one by one. Turning one against the other."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a sense of dread
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They'll look for us..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously doubtful
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They'll never believe that. They saw the creature, they-"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Excitedly awaiting
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They'll soon be ready for you to step onto the flagship."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a hint of playful mischief
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They'll use force if they can, if not, they play on your emotions."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "They're all but ready to crown you a saint."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They're all capable men, I've made sure of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with a hint of sarcasm
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're all nice people, but none of them is you..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Annoyed yet resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're bastards. You don't have to say it. You're safe now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding slightly in understanding
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They're called a lot of things, but my order, we call them voidlings."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Delicately amused
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They're called the Romanov Twins."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a proud, earnest tone
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They're capable soldiers and you need the kinds of guards you can trust with your life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "They're fine people, but I can't be around them for too long, so I like to wander away from the camp."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're gone now. So what is left to be feared?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly stating
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're gone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a curious, concerned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're gone?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sarcastically amused
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "They're gonna hang you for this, thief."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detachedly factual
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They're gonna park an army on every market in Lethram for a week."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Joyfully exclaiming
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They're happy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "They're here somewhere!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They're holdin my ship in Lethram until I come up with the money to pay them back."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Bored indifference
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They're just so bored out of their minds they start meddling with other people's business."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "They're kicking up a real proper storm."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They're more worried about surviving the next winter, or the health of their crop."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly factual
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're mostly on this side."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly, with sorrow
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They're not anymore, Sarah. They might have been once, but you're not their princess anymore."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Incredulously amused
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "They're not going to give a damn if you hang us or not. Gods, they might actually thank you for getting rid of us!"
