msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas...even for me it is not so easy."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas...he...was afraid?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas...what...what are they going to do?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently mocking
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Those Medini have always valued coin over integrity. If the price is right, he'd probably sell them his mother."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those Rosannan men who had previously dared the occasional encounter, voluntary or otherwise, had now grown fearful."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Those are elders, but don't feel too intimidated by them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Those are herbivores, won't harm a fly. And they're none too bright, so not very dangerous at all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those are my breasts!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those are not...they are barely undergarments, let alone clothes!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemnly and reverently
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those are the armies of the Tribes. Khan Hassar's armies."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually confident
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Those are the best days to drink."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Carefully skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "Those are the rumors, my lord. We do not yet have enough evidence to suggest that he has truly united them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Those are the three deaths...the killings."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly revealing
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Those are the three sisters."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Those are transit papers, covering all the required documentation to get you and your soldiers to Mythra."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "Those are typical black, but those others turn a dark purple after a few days."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those around her, until now acceptable, suddenly seemed amateur by comparison."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly curious
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Those bars are as solid as the stones here. Which is saying a lot."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those brave enough to try would settle. Prosper. And like a pig grown fat, slaughtered and eaten by a rival."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively wistful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those days were long gone, and only the desert remained."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hesitant
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those desires that she knew she could control."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, with authority
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Those excercises are just to prepare your body for where it needs to be. A strong body is no replacement for the fundamentals of weapon training."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those families that didn't flee, or failed to, quickly learned that the Tribesmen culture had no understanding of nobility or titles."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hesitant
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those few that dared to quickly glance at their savior."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somberly disappointed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those few that remained were mostly there to hurl a last few insults at the official, before they also left."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily recounting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those few who ran on foot were mostly caught by arrows."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with wonder
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Those forests are old, but they also run deep."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those fortunate were enslaved by humans. Those less fortunate by the orcs."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Those gardens don't put you off?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Those gifted with such divine purpose, find the world often bending to their own will. Their own purpose."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Those girls you've brought along, he's been winning some officers over by giving them away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those girls, they're gossiping."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those halls...my room...the throne...seeing my father and..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a tone of disgust and slight frustration
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Those have been the most poorly maintained, plus, that's where their supply room is."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Frustrated indignation
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Those highborn idiots couldn't see a trap coming if it was spelled out for them!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those impossibly beautiful eyes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those invited seemed confused, looking around for decorations that weren't there."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptical disdain
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Those jungles are full of nasty spores, goblins love to grow their mushrooms there, vile things."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively serious
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Those male slaves chose their lives and safety over their duty to their land and their people."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those most at home to the city conceived of the structure as though it was a beggar in the streets. Consciously noticed, consciously ignored."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Those most essential to their designs are souls of a greater size, and the greater soul dominates the lesser soul."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Firmly confident, commanding
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those of you who cannot bear my command, I give you my word as a princess of the Rose family, that no harm will come to you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Those of you who had the privilege of truly knowing my father, knew how much he enjoyed the winter grace festival."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With resignation, regret
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those parts of her that she had been raised to give to her husband in marriage, now she gave to this old man."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those ravenous eyes that told so much of what they wanted to do to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly confident
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Those roads actually still get patrolled. Quite heavily, actually."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "Those speaking of your beauty, of course."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "Those students who show significant talent in the martial skills are selected from among the others."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a flat, uninterested tone
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Those that could read, of course."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Grimacing in disgust
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that had failed to survive the magical infusion, she threw away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that had not charged into the spearmen, had slowed down too much to perform another charge."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that had survived sat quietly, simply staring into the distance."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Pensively wondering
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that remained all eyed one another."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With weary resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that tried to run were swiftly burned as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With warm appreciation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those things she admired deeply."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those times when she had allowed Lady Carolyn to go too far with her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a coldly detached, sarcastic tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Those two sons-of-bitches would not have thought twice about dragging you into the forest and raping you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those waiting rushed in, those done dancing, rushed out. A frenzied melee."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were a far cry from the kind of legal paperwork that Sarah struggled through."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, with curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were familiar to her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were stories from every corner of the world, and she had often dreamed what they might look like."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Meticulously precise, with reverence
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were the rules everyone lived by, the very rules he knew when he signed the contract."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were the types of terrains that the Tribesmen liked to fight on. Open, spread out."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, somber tone
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "Those who are loyal, are punished."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "Those who can walk outside the ordained paths of history."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who dared to say anything of the sun, the heat, were met only by angry glares."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who fell into its claws were dismissively called Dreamers, for they would stare off into nothingness, disconnected from everything and anyone around them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who gathered knowledge for the sake of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a hint of sly admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had been near the docks were lucky."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly recounting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had been present in the throne room had managed to turn the story of her killing the beast into a tale larger than life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily recalling memories
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had managed to escape the Tribes, had found their homes gone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had the hints of fertility were soon to follow."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "Those who keep their heads down, are left alone."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective and contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "Those who shape the world, rather than be shaped by it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly, with warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who would come upon her could only marvel at her beauty and the rapture of this moment."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Narrow-eyed, cautious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those with the strongest claims fought those who they imagined their most distinct rivals, those with other strong claims."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously warning
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "Those women are gonna eat you alive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those years ago. On the ship."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Frustrated disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Female Soldier"
msgid "Those? Do you even know how to play the game?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Frustrated disbelief
msgctxt "speaker:Male Soldier"
msgid "Those? Do you even know how to play the game?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Gideon needed little encouragement, Sarah felt he still took it in stride, going faster and deeper with each thrust."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mix of anticipation and hesitation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Though I must admit I have received only the invitation, and know little of the topic of the council."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily acknowledging regret
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Though I must admit, until not so long ago, I was made to understand that you were one of the tragic casualties of the Tribes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Founder"
msgid "Though I must admit, you are the first of your lineage to express any magical potency."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively pleased
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Though I must say I enjoyed our conversation."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Though I think this means there won't be any future offspring for the royal family of Bagrad."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah could still hear the sounds of the camp around her, there was some degree of privacy here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah had no doubts that if she had failed to produce a letter, his response would have been a great deal less friendly."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah still had no clothes on, she found it easier to forget her shame when she was busy working."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively somber
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah tried to teach them the small ways of her own people, she could not deny that as they grew, they were children of the tribes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding thoughtfully
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Thomas was late, few complained, after all it was the prerogative of kings to arrive when they wanted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively calm
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though all eyes and hands were on her body, Sarah felt as if there was little she needed to do."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tentatively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though as she grew bigger with each passing day, there were the occasional practical challenges."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though by Sarah's decree she was the head of it, the truth was that the family was a pit of vipers."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though carved from wood, it was unmistakenly a rose. The petals flowed as if they were no different from the real thing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Though considered a base skill, it's actually a rather challenging one; not without risk."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With slight curiosity and attention
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though despite that, Sarah could seem the faint resemblance."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though hard to place, it was impossible to deny that it felt good."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he didn't fill her up, she could feel him hitting the right spots."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he had pulled out, his grip on her body remained, keeping her in place."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he switched between herself and Mary, it was Sarah who he desired most, and it was Sarah that spend most evenings in his bedroom."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In an energetic, playful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he walked, he almost moved as quickly as a man running."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he was older in age, close to fifty Sarah imagined, he had kept himself in strong shape."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he was worn and battered, the armor was relatively well maintained."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually dismissive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he wore a plated armor, he seemed to move as if it weighed nothing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly resolute
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though here, she was just a girl. No title or homeland to speak of."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a calm, sympathetic tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though his expression was stern, Sarah could detect a hint of worry in his face."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though his face and body were marked with scars, nothing about him read as dangerous, or at least not the cruel kind."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though his shoulders still hung low, she hoped that his crown weighed a little less on him now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Though his standing has faded, his reputation among the Eternal Court remains significant."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tentatively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "Though how you did it, well...I look forward to hearing that story some day."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though in theory, any man could promote himself, the truth was that the elections were hardly anything that could be called fair."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it has been years since she was last here, she can walk the hall by memory."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it never quite came natural to her, she learned plenty in time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it raged, in pain at each removal, it raged at anything but her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it seemed near to her, Sarah quickly realized it was an optical illusion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was a fine flower, it possessed nothing that made it dangerous. Or even magical for that part."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was night, the bright moon and a cloudless sky cast a pale light over everything."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was now close to night, the streets were still full of life."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was slurred beyond comprehension, the voice was familiar enough to her that she knew who it was."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was underground, a soft glow of blueish light filled up the cave."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mix of resignation and relief
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it wasn't easy, she slowly felt the weight of all her circumstances, slip away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a cautiously admiring tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though much of the city filled with awe, there was one element that forever troubled her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though none could say why, everyone could feel the item reverberate. A thing that commanded respect, awe."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly with awe
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though partially ruined, the building still impressed on each of them with its vast size."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she could see neither fully believed her niceties, they still appreciated them. Each smiled."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Anxiously curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she didn't feel unsafe, she didn't want to risk getting lost in the city at night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she doubted her views of the events were quite as simple as his."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation, attentively
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she drank slower than the others, her smaller frame and lighter body ended up suffering nearly as much as them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had always come to know him as a skilled lover, something else possessed him that night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had become quite a bit more relaxed around her, Samayra remained always somewhat anxious."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Surprised awe
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had heard the stories of her father and seen the drawings in her picture book, Sarah still felt her breath stolen from her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had managed to make some progress on her own, she realized that Metis' instruction was invaluable."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Quietly perplexed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had met with Maeiv a few times now, she had in truth not truly gotten to know her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had set out with a clear goal, it wasn't long before Sarah found herself starting to become distracted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously anticipating, yet uncertain
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she looked forward to learning a new skill, Sarah wasn't all to sure what to make of the man himself."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively, with a hint of disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she might have enjoyed it, Sarah had no illusions that these men were here for their own relief."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a reflective tone, contemplative expression
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she now realized, that was likely not permanent either, after the fall."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she spoke not their language, she knew well enough they were talking about her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she was angry at herself for not finishing the job, she was more eager for the relief."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she was heading home, her mind kept wandering back to where she had come from."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she was his by right, property in their society, she could feel in his every touch that he loved her as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she wasn't afraid of confined spaces, a place like this still made her nervous."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she would deny it later, when the dreamstalk wore off, she knew that in this moment, she was utterly his."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a detached, analytical tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she'd lived in Lethram for a good few years by now, the truth was that her life played out in predictable patterns."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a hint of nostalgia and warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the angle changed, she felt herself only growing harder."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with a sense of awe
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the castle grew quiet, Sarah felt her own heart beating in her chest so loudly she imagined it might burst through."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the city was strong, it was definitely not strong enough to defeat the larger powers of the world."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly acknowledging harsh reality
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the climate had grown softer, the temperature was still low."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Though the details remain many and varied, with which I will not bore all of you, we must however still settle on the broad points."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm confidence
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the first few missed her, Samayra grew increasingly accurate with each throw."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the house provided for them in many ways, it seemed still limited in the more basic necessities."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily attentive
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the house was silent, it was the kind that pounded on one's ears like a hammer."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the material was coarse, she found the design of it quite pretty."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a weary, longing sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the night drew long, sleep only came for them when all three had long grown exhausted."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Somber contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the pieces of Thomas were now back together, he was like a mirror shattered, impossible to be truly made whole again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the pleasure of it deepend, it also brought back a rush of sanity."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the price had risen, something about supply and demand."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Resignedly accepting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the soldiers of the mercenary company had taken the lake for the miracle that it was, and had thrown plenty of praise on her, Sarah still struggled with it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently with pride
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the song was again from the Union Kingdoms, and the dance steps an odd mixture of that and Lethram, Samayra navigated it all."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the two of them were closely matched, their styles could not be more different."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the vastness of it impressed her, Sarah also saw the ruin of this place."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tinge of heartfelt gratitude
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though the work was hard, Sarah found a certain gratitude in doing it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a weary, resigned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though these bottles were of a lower quality, by now, each was too drunk to notice or care."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tight-lipped skepticism
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though they always remained wary of Belmont and his more coarse behavior, they eventually settled on trusting Sarah's judgement."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though they had only gone there for a few hours, he had still taken the time to prepare her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though they had spend more than a week together, the two met one another for the first time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Slightly disappointed yet amused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though they spend hours more, exploring together, the truth was that Sarah hardly remembered any of it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though they were made of wood, they might as well have been made from steel, given how solid they were."
