msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "We...we could just go somewhere else if it's any trouble..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sorrowfully reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "We...we did..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflecting thoughtful contemplation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "We...we have to..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disheartened resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "We...we lost...because...because..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With cautious optimism
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "We...we'll just have to trust that he has a plan. Who knows, maybe it will all work out like it always does."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "We...we're not at war, are we?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "We...we...had a session today, right? Wanna go train?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a curious, slightly amused whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "We?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a curious, slightly amused whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "We?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Weak enough to be their puppet. Liked enough by the townsfolk to be taken serious."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a trembling, pleading whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weak, begging to be broken."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Softly, with gentle resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Weak."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a defeated and sorrowful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weakened and humiliated, Sarah tried to look away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a resigned whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weakened as she was, she offered little resistance to the strong soldiers that held her down."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Weakened? How? Our city hasn't been attacked in...I don't even know how long."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a resigned tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weakness as they watched their wives, sisters and daughters be taken by the conquerors."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cautiously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Wealth and women in particular."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiring respect
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Wealth then. I will pay you and your men a price for a peaceful withdrawal. You can take your spoils and ride back to the desert."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued and reflective
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Wealth, power, love."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Wealth. Women. Land."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Wear the dress"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a weary, tired tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Wearing only her underwear, she climbed into bed. The day's events had exhausted her."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Wearing the same slave outfit as her, Sarah instantly knew what the woman was."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a nostalgic, wistful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weaving between narrow alleys and high buildings, it was almost like the sun was being drowned out."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weaving her fingers, she gently produced and guided the magical energies into the seedling."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weaving through the many busy streets and narrow alleys, he guided her towards his house."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weaving through the small camps, Sarah finally found her way back to the campfire where she had left Samayra."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weaving through the twists and bends of the dunes, Sarah could slowly hear the world grow quieter."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reluctantly sharing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Week had gone by since her brother had been taken hostage by Marion."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weeks more had passed, and by now, the day of the exam had drawn close."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously hesitant
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Weeks to decide, perhaps only months to implement these changes before the attack comes."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tone of hopeful anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weeks, months, years."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Weighing down on her, Sarah felt her arms buckle, crashing fast first into the ground."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Welcomingly with warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "Welcome, child."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With polite formality and welcoming warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Welcome, each of you, to today's council meeting."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Welcoming with joy and warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Priest"
msgid "Welcome, friends and family, to this most blessed day."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Officer"
msgid "Welcome, you are the mercenary company, I imagine?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Welcomingly embracing
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "Welcome."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Excitedly proclaiming
msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "Well Gods, ain't no better Inn than the Dunstin Inn."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cynically amused
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Well I don't pay you to think, blondie."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Well I knew when I took that job years back to ship you across the sea that you were a strange one."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Playfully teasing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well I love fish."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Sternly unimpressed
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well I mean that a Tribesmen just shows up and tells them they want something, and they call it a tax."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "Well I mean that just because you're a slave, doesn't mean you have to act like you're an imbecile."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well I suppose that's half the fun, isn't it? Magical botany is nothing if not surprising."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly admonishing
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Well I told you the price had gone up, and you kept agreeing and wanted it added to your tab."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative, slightly hesitant tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well I wouldn't go that far."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well I'm glad to hear that."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, yet subtly menacing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well I'm in charge, so you might actually get in trouble of you don't show up."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a disbelieving, wide-eyed tone
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well I've seen men trying to buy me for a night in exchange for some food and something to drink."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Triumphantly declaring
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well I, great basilisk, fear nothing! If you will not give my beloved back to me, I shall set her free myself!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Well all put together, I suspect...the bill is quite a bit more than what you have on you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently encouraging
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Well better work fast then, unless you wanna be out here on your knees all night."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Solemnly, with resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well don't."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: "Contentedly satisfied"
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well done for now, Gideon."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "Well done, Dalia, as always."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "Well done, Sarah."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Well done, girl!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Well earned, thought Sarah."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Well endowed, she did her best to fit all of him into her mouth, and partially her throat."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a calm, dismissive tone
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Well even I'm afraid of a basilisk, so you're crazy if you're not."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well everyone has seen I didn't do nothin but talk to a few pretty girls."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Well get on the wagon then."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, with assurance
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Well go on then. I didn't tell you to stop working."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In an amused, self-deprecating tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well guess I'm even richer now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "Well if the girl can find it in herself to stay, then I'd be a mighty coward if I was the one to walk away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well if you truly shifted yourself into such a form, you would entirely become it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With amused curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "Well it is your house, so your rules I suppose."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well it sounds like you want to say something."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well it wasn't you, now was it?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally impressed
msgctxt "speaker:King Orwell Rose"
msgid "Well it's a little like dancing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well it's been a while since I've drawn my sword, and it's getting rusty."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Conveying a sense of reluctant resignation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well it's the only option we have."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously uncertain
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Well it's the truth. Before you, there was nobody, and after you..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well it's...different..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "Well my name is Matthew, but you can call me officer Matt, got that?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Cheerfully excited
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Well now, that will be a sight to see."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Well said, Sarah."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Well situated between the crossroads of various civilizations, Lethram was a rare beacon of independence."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a tone of seasoned confidence
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Well supplied and guided by the skilled navigators of the Mythran Empire, they faced little dangers from the desert."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worried yet tenderly affectionate
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Well then you've made a very big mistake, because so long as you live, you're mine."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually dismissing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well then, I was going to go over the basics some more, but we can skip a few lessons."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly, confidently
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Well then, let us settle this deal."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a mix of encouragement and slight urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Well then, let's get you started with the first shift."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With growing concern and urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Well then. Shall we? Before we lose precious daylight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Well trained by now, Sarah knew what came after as well."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well what if you kill my brother? Then who will inherit the throne after him?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Excitedly, with amazement
msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "Well what? I found her! I get first."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a skeptical tone
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Well where then?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With a condescending smirk
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Well whoever told you that must have been an idiot."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a reflective, slightly amused tone
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well yeah, but that's just my winning personality. You're the one who turned down an invitation. That's cold."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a resigned, weary tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I ain't going anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutrally informative
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Well, I ain't like them, I can tell you that much."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reluctantly admitting defeat
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well, I ain't the one that can shoot fire from my hands. If this goes sideways, it's my ass that's on the line."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I can always get dressed again if that's what you want."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily amused
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well, I can pretty much control when I do or don't finish, so unless you wanna be here all night, I suggest you move that pretty face up close."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a playful teasing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Well, I can't exactly refuse an order from my new boss, right?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "Well, I can't promise that's gonna stay like that forever."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Adoringly remembering
msgctxt "speaker:Damian"
msgid "Well, I did as Sir Goderic asked and begged him to teach me how to fight."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a playful, teasing manner
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Well, I didn't pay a cent for this bottle myself, so it would feel rude to charge you."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a stern, resolute tone
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I don't like to yell, but I'll keep yelling at you until one day you might actually believe me."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Suspiciously questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I don't think they serve the quality stuff you're used to."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Worriedly anticipating rest
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I fear we have already spoken for so long. The hour draws late and I should really retire."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disappointedly apologetic
msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "Well, I feel that I have taken up enough of your time."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I guess in that case I'll need a guide."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually concluding
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I guess that's that then."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily curious, yet hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Well, I had told you that I was looking forward to meeting you ever since I first heard the rumors. Ever since I suspected you might still be alive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With hopeful enthusiasm
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I have some good news in case you need cheering up."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, with pride
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Well, I have worked here long enough. They are far from rumors."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "Well, I haven't heard of any orders coming from him either, so whatever he's doing in there, it doesn't seem to do much for the company."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I hope I've impressed. If there is no more business then..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a concerned yet cautious tone
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I hoped it wouldn't have to come to this, but if you're going to keep lying I'll have to do a strip search."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calmly reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "Well, I imagine there might a few ways you could make it up to us."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I know a few ways."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Contemplatively acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Well, I know that the council is a prestigious position. And I know that there have not often been people of my...station, allowed to attend."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I managed to get myself into plenty of trouble lately. But the thing from today that was..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Flatly detached
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I mean, that's between a man and his wife, none of my business."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I mean, you don't have to go right away."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nodding enthusiastically
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I mean...you know some magic right?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually confident, with a slight edge
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Well, I meant what I said. You can have anything you want, so I guess that includes this one."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warily anticipating the next phrase
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "Well, I never had all the things you lost to begin with, and instead of eyes preying on me, I had the opposite."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I paid for the night, didn't I?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Frustrated exasperation
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I spend all my life in a palace, locked up. I don't want to be locked up here, reading more books!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I suppose I should give you something to do then."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confusedly uncertain
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Well, I suppose that puts us a bit at odds here."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Calm curiosity, slightly amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I suppose there are worse names, should it stick."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively satisfied
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Well, I suppose we've reached the end of our road."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently amused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I suspect you're virile enough."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "Well, I think I understand. We all have to do things sometimes. To survive."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflectively sorrowful
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I think I'll be sad to see you leave."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Concerned yet reassuring
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Well, I think it's time for you to head back to camp."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I think that..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Encouragingly supportive
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I think you have a good base to get started on, but you'll need to build some muscle, as well as learn some technique."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I think you owe me now. It's only fair."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I told you about when I ran away from home."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Well, I took to magic early and was recruited to join the Circle."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I was a lot younger."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Well, I was born around three-hundred years ago."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Well, I was one too. I suspect we both made a mistake we're now paying for."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Well, I was plannin on takin you somewhere fancy, but that was before I saw you in this dress..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Nervously recounting a past success
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Well, I was the commander that broke the insurrectionist army."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Disinterestedly acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Well, I wasn't asking for your opinion, it's already been decided. You're going."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Thoughtfully intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Well, I women have other skills I suppose. Some equally, if not more dangerous than sword."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a playful, teasing manner
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Well, I worry. Even when I don't have to."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I wouldn't call what you have nothing."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a light-hearted, playful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Well, I'd be a rather poor bodyguard if I wasn't."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Playfully teasing
msgctxt "speaker:Female Soldier"
msgid "Well, I'd gladly roll around in the hay with you too."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I'd like to get to know all your friends. Maybe we can meet up with him another time?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently, with a hint of sarcasm
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I'd love to play secretary with you, but I can't read or write for shit."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Well, I'll be off then."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective, thoughtful delivery
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, I'll forgive you. I guess there are worse ways to die than between your legs."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I'll pass the exam, and then I'll join...but...what then?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well, I'll teach you. And maybe we can get you to unwind while we're at it."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "Well, I'll tell you two lies about myself, and one truth, and you can guess which is the truth."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well, I'm a mage with a fair bit of experience."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Jacob"
msgid "Well, I'm busy right now."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I'm certain there is a bedroom available for you somewhere in the house. You are more than welcome as my guest."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confidently and warmly
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I'm certain there is a bedroom available for you somewhere in the house. You are more than welcome as our guest."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I'm glad to see you're carrying it well, Thomas."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With restrained excitement
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I'm going to keep you to it anyway."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Well, I'm here now anyway. And I can't say I'm in much of a hurry to return to that whole affair."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a playful exasperation
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Well, I'm just saying that when I took you on as my sworn servant, I was expecting a man, not a whiny little girl!"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Skeptically bemused
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I'm not really looking for you to fulfill your general's duties..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Confusedly pondering
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Well, I'm not so sure you deserve all the credit there. Don't your generals deserve some?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reflective concern
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well, I'm not sure if you've heard, but the good people of Lethram, myself included, have found ourselves homeless."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Admiringly knowledgeable
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well, I'm quite proficient with Botany and Transmogrification."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: With resigned hopefulness
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well, I'm sad to see our encounter cut so short, but I'm sure we will meet again."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, I'm sure you have other affairs to see to. You strike me as a busy man."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Well, I've got some things that can make time go by a whole lot more pleasant."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Intrigued, with curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, Medini has long relied on mercenaries to fight their battles for them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Reluctantly admitting
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, Ridgehaven was one of the towns where I stayed for a while as I was drifting from place to place."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well, Samayra, I think it would be best if we go back to my room."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, Sarah, I need to go meet up with some of my men, I promised I'd play bone-dice with them."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Well, Sarah, I think you're right about a problem."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:The Official"
msgid "Well, Sarah, a pleasure to have made your acquaintance."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "Well, Sarah, how about you fuck back off to your own cell?"
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Casually intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "Well, Sarah, maybe the solution would be if instead of me and Caleb having some private time for the two of us..."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "Well, Sarah, my name is Eula."
msgstr ""

#. emotion: In a contemplative and mildly amused tone
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Well, Sarah, not so different from what the other creature tried to do when it spoke to you."
msgstr ""

